"content":"Use a different local SoftHSM chart"},"174":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/deployment/self-hosted/fastlane-96","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/deployment/self-hosted/fastlane","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/deployment/self-hosted/fastlane#command-line-options","content":"Fastlane does not provide an offline mode. Use the manual Helm workflow and a prepared registry/chart mirror for disconnected environments."},"175":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/deployment/self-hosted/fastlane-97","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/deployment/self-hosted/fastlane","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/deployment/self-hosted/fastlane#development-mode","content":"`--development` adjusts the Keycloak `lamassu` realm generated by Fastlane for a disposable evaluation environment:"},"176":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/deployment/self-hosted/fastlane-98","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/deployment/self-hosted/fastlane","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/deployment/self-hosted/fastlane#development-mode","content":"the `lamassu` user is fully provisioned (first name Lamassu, last name Admin, email `lamassu@lamassu.io`, verified): there are no profile setup or password change steps on first login"},"177":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/deployment/self-hosted/fastlane-99","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/deployment/self-hosted/fastlane","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/deployment/self-hosted/fastlane#development-mode","content":"the well-known `lamassu`/`lamassu` password is fixed and permanent: it is never rotated and grants the `pki-admin` role, including non-interactive tokens through the `frontend` client"},"178":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/deployment/self-hosted/fastlane-100","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/deployment/self-hosted/fastlane","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/deployment/self-hosted/fastlane#development-mode","content":"the `frontend` client accepts any redirect URI and any web origin (`*`) instead of the original `/*` patterns"},"179":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/deployment/self-hosted/fastlane-101","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/deployment/self-hosted/fastlane","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/deployment/self-hosted/fastlane#development-mode","content":"With `--development`, the fixed `lamassu`/`lamassu` password grants `pki-admin` access to anyone who can reach the installation. Never use it on anything exposed beyond a development machine or a network-reachable host."},"180":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/deployment/self-hosted/fastlane-102","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/deployment/self-hosted/fastlane","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/deployment/self-hosted/fastlane#development-mode","content":"`--development` applies when the `lamassu` realm is first imported. It does not modify an existing cluster. It can be combined with `--sample-data`: the development transform runs first, then sample data is added to the same realm configuration."},"181":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/deployment/self-hosted/fastlane-103","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/deployment/self-hosted/fastlane","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/deployment/self-hosted/fastlane#what-the-script-configures","content":"Fastlane:"},"182":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/deployment/self-hosted/fastlane-104","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/deployment/self-hosted/fastlane","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/deployment/self-hosted/fastlane#what-the-script-configures","content":"validates local tools and the selected cluster"},"183":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/deployment/self-hosted/fastlane-105","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/deployment/self-hosted/fastlane","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/deployment/self-hosted/fastlane#what-the-script-configures","content":"installs or upgrades Envoy Gateway 1.8 and creates the `eg` `GatewayClass`"},"184":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/deployment/self-hosted/fastlane-106","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/deployment/self-hosted/fastlane","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/deployment/self-hosted/fastlane#what-the-script-configures","content":"creates the namespace"},"185":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/deployment/self-hosted/fastlane-107","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/deployment/self-hosted/fastlane","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/deployment/self-hosted/fastlane#what-the-script-configures","content":"installs PostgreSQL and creates the required databases"},"186":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/deployment/self-hosted/fastlane-108","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/deployment/self-hosted/fastlane","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/deployment/self-hosted/fastlane#what-the-script-configures","content":"installs Keycloak and creates the `lamassu` realm, frontend client, admin role and initial user"},"187":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/deployment/self-hosted/fastlane-109","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/deployment/self-hosted/fastlane","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/deployment/self-hosted/fastlane#what-the-script-configures","content":"installs RabbitMQ"},"188":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/deployment/self-hosted/fastlane-110","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/deployment/self-hosted/fastlane","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/deployment/self-hosted/fastlane#what-the-script-configures","content":"optionally installs observability and lab HSM components"},"189":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/deployment/self-hosted/fastlane-111","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/deployment/self-hosted/fastlane","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/deployment/self-hosted/fastlane#what-the-script-configures","content":"generates `lamassu.yaml` and installs the Lamassu chart"},"190":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/deployment/self-hosted/fastlane-112","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/deployment/self-hosted/fastlane","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/deployment/self-hosted/fastlane#what-the-script-configures","content":"optionally loads sample data"},"191":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/deployment/self-hosted/fastlane-113","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/deployment/self-hosted/fastlane","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/deployment/self-hosted/fastlane#what-the-script-configures","content":"The generated configuration exposes Keycloak at `/auth` through the same Gateway and bootstraps the initial `lamassu` user as a Lamassu super administrator."},"192":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/deployment/self-hosted/fastlane-114","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/deployment/self-hosted/fastlane","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/deployment/self-hosted/fastlane#tls-behavior","content":"With both `--tls-crt` and `--tls-key`, Fastlane creates the `downstream-provided-crt` Secret and configures `tls.type: external`."},"193":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/deployment/self-hosted/fastlane-115","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/deployment/self-hosted/fastlane","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/deployment/self-hosted/fastlane#tls-behavior","content":"Without them, it configures cert-manager with a self-signed issuer. This is suitable for a lab but will not be trusted by clients until you distribute the CA. Use Helm when you need a corporate Issuer, public ACME issuer or an existing Secret managed by another system."},"194":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/deployment/self-hosted/fastlane-116","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/deployment/self-hosted/fastlane","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/deployment/self-hosted/fastlane#credentials-and-generated-files","content":"Non-interactive mode generates random PostgreSQL, RabbitMQ and Keycloak administrator passwords. The initial Lamassu login is `lamassu` / `lamassu` and requires a password change on first use, unless `--development` was used: in that case the password stays fixed and permanent."},"195":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/deployment/self-hosted/fastlane-117","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/deployment/self-hosted/fastlane","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/deployment/self-hosted/fastlane#credentials-and-generated-files","content":"Fastlane writes `lamassu.yaml` in the current directory and injects credentials into it."},"196":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/deployment/self-hosted/fastlane-118","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/deployment/self-hosted/fastlane","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/deployment/self-hosted/fastlane#credentials-and-generated-files","content":"Protect the generated values file, record the generated credentials in an appropriate secret store and do not reuse the evaluation identity setup in production."},"197":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/deployment/self-hosted/fastlane-119","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/deployment/self-hosted/fastlane","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/deployment/self-hosted/fastlane#verify-the-installation","content":"Then open `https://pki.example.com` and sign in with the initial user. If the Gateway is programmed but the URL is unreachable, follow the checks in Expose the Gateway."},"198":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/deployment/self-hosted/helm","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/deployment/self-hosted/helm","type":"page","content":"Install with Helm","breadcrumbs":["Docs","Deployment","Kubernetes self-managed"],"tags":[],"url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/deployment/self-hosted/helm"},"199":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/deployment/self-hosted/helm-0","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/deployment/self-hosted/helm","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/deployment/self-hosted/helm","content":"Prepare dependencies, configure the Lamassu chart and verify a controlled Kubernetes deployment."},"200":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/deployment/self-hosted/helm-1","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/deployment/self-hosted/helm","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/deployment/self-hosted/helm#install-lamassu-with-helm","content":"Install Lamassu with Helm"},"201":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/deployment/self-hosted/helm-2","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/deployment/self-hosted/helm","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/deployment/self-hosted/helm#before-you-begin","content":"Before you begin"},"202":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/deployment/self-hosted/helm-3","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/deployment/self-hosted/helm","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/deployment/self-hosted/helm#1-install-the-gateway-prerequisites","content":"1\\. Install the Gateway prerequisites"},"203":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/deployment/self-hosted/helm-4","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/deployment/self-hosted/helm","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/deployment/self-hosted/helm#2-create-a-values-file","content":"2\\. Create a values file"},"204":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/deployment/self-hosted/helm-5","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/deployment/self-hosted/helm","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/deployment/self-hosted/helm#tls-with-an-existing-secret","content":"TLS with an existing Secret"},"205":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/deployment/self-hosted/helm-6","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/deployment/self-hosted/helm","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/deployment/self-hosted/helm#amqp-tls-amqps","content":"AMQP TLS (AMQPS)"},"206":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/deployment/self-hosted/helm-7","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/deployment/self-hosted/helm","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/deployment/self-hosted/helm#provision-the-first-administrator","content":"Provision the first administrator"},"207":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/deployment/self-hosted/helm-8","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/deployment/self-hosted/helm","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/deployment/self-hosted/helm#3-install-lamassu","content":"3\\. Install Lamassu"},"208":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/deployment/self-hosted/helm-9","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/deployment/self-hosted/helm","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/deployment/self-hosted/helm#4-verify-the-deployment","content":"4\\. Verify the deployment"},"209":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/deployment/self-hosted/helm-10","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/deployment/self-hosted/helm","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/deployment/self-hosted/helm#upgrading-lamassu","content":"Upgrading Lamassu"},"210":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/deployment/self-hosted/helm-11","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/deployment/self-hosted/helm","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/deployment/self-hosted/helm#production-decisions","content":"Production decisions"},"211":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/deployment/self-hosted/helm-12","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/deployment/self-hosted/helm","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/deployment/self-hosted/helm#install-lamassu-with-helm","content":"Use the Helm workflow when you need explicit control over identity, databases, messaging, certificates, storage and upgrades. For an evaluation environment where the script can make those choices for you, use Fastlane."},"212":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/deployment/self-hosted/helm-13","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/deployment/self-hosted/helm","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/deployment/self-hosted/helm#before-you-begin","content":"Prepare the platform services that are deliberately outside the Lamassu chart:"},"213":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/deployment/self-hosted/helm-14","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/deployment/self-hosted/helm","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/deployment/self-hosted/helm#before-you-begin","content":"a Kubernetes 1.24+ cluster and Helm 3.2+"},"214":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/deployment/self-hosted/helm-15","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/deployment/self-hosted/helm","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/deployment/self-hosted/helm#before-you-begin","content":"a reachable PostgreSQL server and a role allowed to create databases and schemas"},"215":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/deployment/self-hosted/helm-16","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/deployment/self-hosted/helm","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/deployment/self-hosted/helm#before-you-begin","content":"a reachable RabbitMQ broker and credentials"},"216":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/deployment/self-hosted/helm-17","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/deployment/self-hosted/helm","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/deployment/self-hosted/helm#before-you-begin","content":"an OIDC provider, normally Keycloak, with a realm/tenant and client for Lamassu"},"217":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/deployment/self-hosted/helm-18","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/deployment/self-hosted/helm","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/deployment/self-hosted/helm#before-you-begin","content":"Envoy Gateway 1.8+ and a `GatewayClass`"},"218":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/deployment/self-hosted/helm-19","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/deployment/self-hosted/helm","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/deployment/self-hosted/helm#before-you-begin","content":"cert-manager 1.14+ (only for the default `tls.type: certManager` mode); for trusted TLS, either a trusted issuer or a Kubernetes TLS Secret"},"219":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/deployment/self-hosted/helm-20","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/deployment/self-hosted/helm","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/deployment/self-hosted/helm#before-you-begin","content":"a StorageClass and an external traffic design"},"220":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/deployment/self-hosted/helm-21","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/deployment/self-hosted/helm","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/deployment/self-hosted/helm#before-you-begin","content":"The chart defaults to a `GatewayClass` named `eg`. Change `gateway.className` if your platform team uses another name."},"221":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/deployment/self-hosted/helm-22","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/deployment/self-hosted/helm","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/deployment/self-hosted/helm#before-you-begin","content":"You provide the PostgreSQL server. The chart's pre-install job connects with the supplied credentials, creates the required `pki`, `authz` and `wfx` databases and service schemas, runs migrations, and applies `services.authz.bootstrap`."},"222":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/deployment/self-hosted/helm-23","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/deployment/self-hosted/helm","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/deployment/self-hosted/helm#before-you-begin","content":"The chart has no Helm dependencies that install PostgreSQL, RabbitMQ, an OIDC provider, Envoy Gateway or cert-manager."},"223":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/deployment/self-hosted/helm-24","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/deployment/self-hosted/helm","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/deployment/self-hosted/helm#1-install-the-gateway-prerequisites","content":"Install or upgrade the Envoy Gateway CRDs before its controller. The commands below match the version used by the Lamassu Helm repository:"},"224":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/deployment/self-hosted/helm-25","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/deployment/self-hosted/helm","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/deployment/self-hosted/helm#1-install-the-gateway-prerequisites","content":"Create the default `GatewayClass` if it does not already exist. Save this manifest as `gateway-class.yaml`:"},"225":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/deployment/self-hosted/helm-26","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/deployment/self-hosted/helm","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/deployment/self-hosted/helm#1-install-the-gateway-prerequisites","content":"Install cert-manager separately before Lamassu, but only for the default `tls.type: certManager` mode. In that mode the chart renders its self-signed Issuer and CA Certificate resources regardless of whether `tls.certManagerOptions.clusterIssuer` is set, so cert-manager stays a prerequisite. With `tls.type: external`, the chart renders no cert-manager resources and the Gateway terminates TLS with an existing Secret you provide instead."},"226":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/deployment/self-hosted/helm-27","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/deployment/self-hosted/helm","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/deployment/self-hosted/helm#2-create-a-values-file","content":"Start with the chart defaults and override the environment-specific values. This example assumes PostgreSQL, RabbitMQ and Keycloak are reachable through Kubernetes DNS, and exposes Keycloak at `/auth` through the shared Lamassu Gateway:"},"227":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/deployment/self-hosted/helm-28","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/deployment/self-hosted/helm","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/deployment/self-hosted/helm#2-create-a-values-file","content":"Do not add `gateway.addresses` by default. Leave address assignment to the load-balancer implementation unless your network design requires a specific Kubernetes-side VIP. The public IP of an upstream NAT gateway or reverse proxy does not belong in this value."},"228":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/deployment/self-hosted/helm-29","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/deployment/self-hosted/helm","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/deployment/self-hosted/helm#2-create-a-values-file","content":"If Keycloak is external and already has its own reachable URL, point the OIDC settings at it and omit the `/auth` entry from `gateway.extraRouting`."},"229":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/deployment/self-hosted/helm-30","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/deployment/self-hosted/helm","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/deployment/self-hosted/helm#2-create-a-values-file","content":"If your values file still carries the legacy gateway JWT validation settings — `auth.oidc.apiGateway.jwks`, `auth.authorization.rolesClaim` or `auth.authorization.roles.admin` — remove them. The migration guide `charts/lamassu/CHANGELOG/3.8.0->4.0.0.md` documents their removal with no compatibility aliases, and `values.schema.json` rejects the leftover blocks instead of silently ignoring them. The replacements are `services.authz.jwkUrl` and `services.authz.bootstrap`, already shown in the example above."},"230":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/deployment/self-hosted/helm-31","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/deployment/self-hosted/helm","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/deployment/self-hosted/helm#tls-with-an-existing-secret","content":"Create a Secret containing `tls.crt` and `tls.key`, then reference it. The Secret must already exist before installing: in `external` mode the chart renders no cert-manager resources and never creates this Secret."},"231":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/deployment/self-hosted/helm-32","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/deployment/self-hosted/helm","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/deployment/self-hosted/helm#amqp-tls-amqps","content":"`amqp.tls: true` selects AMQPS in every event-bus configuration block. The default port stays `5672` and does not change automatically when TLS is enabled, so set `amqp.port` to the broker's TLS listener, commonly `5671`."},"232":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/deployment/self-hosted/helm-33","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/deployment/self-hosted/helm","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/deployment/self-hosted/helm#amqp-tls-amqps","content":"With no CA Secret configured, the event-bus clients use the system-trusted CAs. To trust a private CA, create a Secret in the release namespace containing the CA certificate in PEM format and set `amqp.ca.secretName` (and `amqp.ca.certificateKey` if the data key is not `ca.crt`)."},"233":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/deployment/self-hosted/helm-34","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/deployment/self-hosted/helm","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/deployment/self-hosted/helm#amqp-tls-amqps","content":"For brokers that require mutual TLS, create a Secret containing the client certificate and private key and set `amqp.client.secretName` (with `amqp.client.certificateKey` and `amqp.client.privateKeyKey` if the data keys are not `tls.crt` and `tls.key`)."},"234":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/deployment/self-hosted/helm-35","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/deployment/self-hosted/helm","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/deployment/self-hosted/helm#amqp-tls-amqps","content":"The chart mounts configured Secrets read-only into every AMQP-consuming workload: the CA certificate under `/etc/lamassu/amqp/ca` and the client certificate and key under `/etc/lamassu/amqp/client`. The mounted file names are always `ca.crt`, `tls.crt` and `tls.key` — the `certificateKey` and `privateKeyKey` values rename only the Secret data keys, never the on-disk paths. The client private key is mounted with restrictive permissions (`defaultMode: 0440`; the CA volume uses `0444`), which works because the chart adds `fsGroup` to the pod security context when `amqp.client.secretName` is set — it uses the container `runAsGroup` (default `65532`) when `fsGroup` is not already set."},"235":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/deployment/self-hosted/helm-36","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/deployment/self-hosted/helm","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/deployment/self-hosted/helm#amqp-tls-amqps","content":"Both Secret options require `amqp.tls: true`: `values.schema.json` rejects a non-empty `secretName` when `tls` is false, rejects unknown keys and rejects data-key names outside `^[A-Za-z0-9._-]+$`. The referenced Secret must exist in the release namespace or the consuming pods fail to start."},"236":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/deployment/self-hosted/helm-37","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/deployment/self-hosted/helm","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/deployment/self-hosted/helm#amqp-tls-amqps","content":"The AMQP client loads certificates at startup, so restart the consuming pods after updating either Secret. Changing any `amqp` value rolls the consuming pods through the `checksum/config` annotation, but a change to Secret content alone does not trigger a rollout."},"237":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/deployment/self-hosted/helm-38","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/deployment/self-hosted/helm","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/deployment/self-hosted/helm#amqp-tls-amqps","content":"Per the migration guide `charts/lamassu/CHANGELOG/3.8.0->4.0.0.md`: in 3.8.0 `amqp.tls` was not applied and event-bus clients used plaintext AMQP; from 4.0.0, `amqp.tls: true` switches them to AMQPS. Set `amqp.port` to the broker TLS listener before upgrading, or set `amqp.tls: false` to keep plaintext AMQP. `amqp.tls: false` sends the broker credentials and all event-bus traffic in cleartext."},"238":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/deployment/self-hosted/helm-39","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/deployment/self-hosted/helm","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/deployment/self-hosted/helm#provision-the-first-administrator","content":"There is no implicit superuser. Create the role or group expected by `services.authz.bootstrap` in the OIDC provider and assign it to at least one administrator before exposing Lamassu."},"239":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/deployment/self-hosted/helm-40","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/deployment/self-hosted/helm","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/deployment/self-hosted/helm#provision-the-first-administrator","content":"The pre-install and pre-upgrade job applies the bootstrap idempotently: existing principals are preserved and missing grants are added."},"240":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/deployment/self-hosted/helm-41","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/deployment/self-hosted/helm","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/deployment/self-hosted/helm#provision-the-first-administrator","content":"Test both an authorized identity and a denied identity. If no token matches an active bootstrap principal, nobody can administer the PKI."},"241":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/deployment/self-hosted/helm-42","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/deployment/self-hosted/helm","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/deployment/self-hosted/helm#provision-the-first-administrator","content":"See Access control for the principal and policy model."},"242":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/deployment/self-hosted/helm-43","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/deployment/self-hosted/helm","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/deployment/self-hosted/helm#3-install-lamassu","content":"To install a local checkout instead:"},"243":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/deployment/self-hosted/helm-44","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/deployment/self-hosted/helm","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/deployment/self-hosted/helm#4-verify-the-deployment","content":"The Gateway should report `PROGRAMMED=True`. If it is programmed but has no usable address, continue with Expose the Gateway."},"244":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/deployment/self-hosted/helm-45","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/deployment/self-hosted/helm","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/deployment/self-hosted/helm#4-verify-the-deployment","content":"The Helm test checks the CA, DMS Manager, Device Manager and VA health endpoints and verifies the UI response."},"245":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/deployment/self-hosted/helm-46","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/deployment/self-hosted/helm","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/deployment/self-hosted/helm#upgrading-lamassu","content":"Version-specific upgrade steps live in `charts/lamassu/CHANGELOG/` in the Helm repository. The chart also ships an optional pre-upgrade Job that migrates existing CA private keys into the KMS engine configured for the release. It is off by default (`migrations.caToKms.enabled: false`) and is only needed when upgrading from a version prior to 3.7.0."},"246":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/deployment/self-hosted/helm-47","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/deployment/self-hosted/helm","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/deployment/self-hosted/helm#upgrading-lamassu","content":"While the flag is enabled, every `helm upgrade` creates the `<chart fullname>-ca-to-kms-migration` Job (`lamassu-ca-to-kms-migration` for release `lamassu`); a fresh install does not create it. Its hook weight is `-10`, so it runs before the other pre-upgrade hooks: the authorization bootstrap configuration (weight `-4`) and the database-migration Job (weight `-3`)."},"247":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/deployment/self-hosted/helm-48","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/deployment/self-hosted/helm","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/deployment/self-hosted/helm#upgrading-lamassu","content":"The Job consumes the same KMS service configuration the chart renders into the KMS ConfigMap, including the engines from `services.kms.cryptoEngines`, and runs the migration tool defined in `migrations.caToKms.image`. It mounts that configuration read-only at `/etc/lamassuiot/config.yml` from the ConfigMap key `config`, so configure the destination engine in your values before the upgrade that performs the migration."},"248":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/deployment/self-hosted/helm-49","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/deployment/self-hosted/helm","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/deployment/self-hosted/helm#upgrading-lamassu","content":"The Job resolves its configuration through a projected volume with two optional sources: the release-scoped `<chart fullname>-kms-config` (`lamassu-kms-config` for release `lamassu`, `prod-lamassu-kms-config` for release `prod`) and the legacy unscoped `kms-config` created by chart versions before release-scoped naming. The legacy configuration remains authoritative while it is still present, and the release-scoped one is used once the legacy one is gone. Both sources are optional, so a missing ConfigMap never leaves the upgrade pod in `ContainerCreating`."},"249":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/deployment/self-hosted/helm-50","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/deployment/self-hosted/helm","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/deployment/self-hosted/helm#upgrading-lamassu","content":"Keep `migrations.caToKms.enabled: true` for the upgrade that performs the migration, then remove the flag from your values once the migration completes; it defaults to `false`."},"250":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/deployment/self-hosted/helm-51","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/deployment/self-hosted/helm","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/deployment/self-hosted/helm#production-decisions","content":"Before going live, review:"},"251":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/deployment/self-hosted/helm-52","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/deployment/self-hosted/helm","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/deployment/self-hosted/helm#production-decisions","content":"backup and recovery for PostgreSQL and persistent volumes"},"252":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/deployment/self-hosted/helm-53","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/deployment/self-hosted/helm","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/deployment/self-hosted/helm#production-decisions","content":"a production KMS engine; the default filesystem engine is not an HA design"},"253":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/deployment/self-hosted/helm-54","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/deployment/self-hosted/helm","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/deployment/self-hosted/helm#production-decisions","content":"shared VA storage before increasing VA replicas"},"254":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/deployment/self-hosted/helm-55","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/deployment/self-hosted/helm","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/deployment/self-hosted/helm#production-decisions","content":"managed OIDC roles and removal of evaluation credentials"},"255":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/deployment/self-hosted/helm-56","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/deployment/self-hosted/helm","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/deployment/self-hosted/helm#production-decisions","content":"a trusted TLS issuer or externally managed certificate"},"256":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/deployment/self-hosted/helm-57","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/deployment/self-hosted/helm","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/deployment/self-hosted/helm#production-decisions","content":"resource requests, replicas, autoscaling, disruption budgets and placement"},"257":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/deployment/self-hosted/helm-58","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/deployment/self-hosted/helm","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/deployment/self-hosted/helm#production-decisions","content":"SMTP, observability and alert delivery"},"258":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/deployment/self-hosted/helm-59","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/deployment/self-hosted/helm","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/deployment/self-hosted/helm#production-decisions","content":"the version upgrade guides and migration notes in `charts/lamassu/CHANGELOG/` before every upgrade, including the optional CA-to-KMS migration hook described above"},"259":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/deployment/self-hosted/helm-60","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/deployment/self-hosted/helm","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/deployment/self-hosted/helm#production-decisions","content":"The complete values reference is maintained in `charts/lamassu/VALUES.md` in the Helm repository."},"260":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/deployment/self-hosted/networking","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/deployment/self-hosted/networking","type":"page","content":"Expose the Gateway","breadcrumbs":["Docs","Deployment","Kubernetes self-managed"],"tags":[],"url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/deployment/self-hosted/networking"},"261":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/deployment/self-hosted/networking-0","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/deployment/self-hosted/networking","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/deployment/self-hosted/networking","content":"Choose how clients reach Lamassu, when to set gateway.addresses and how to design multiple Gateways."},"262":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/deployment/self-hosted/networking-1","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/deployment/self-hosted/networking","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/deployment/self-hosted/networking#expose-the-lamassu-gateway","content":"Expose the Lamassu Gateway"},"263":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/deployment/self-hosted/networking-2","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/deployment/self-hosted/networking","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/deployment/self-hosted/networking#do-you-need-gatewayaddresses","content":"Do you need `gateway.addresses`?"},"264":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/deployment/self-hosted/networking-3","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/deployment/self-hosted/networking","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/deployment/self-hosted/networking#recommended-single-node-design","content":"Recommended single-node design"},"265":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/deployment/self-hosted/networking-4","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/deployment/self-hosted/networking","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/deployment/self-hosted/networking#k3s","content":"K3s"},"266":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/deployment/self-hosted/networking-5","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/deployment/self-hosted/networking","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/deployment/self-hosted/networking#bare-metal-with-metallb-or-kube-vip","content":"Bare metal with MetalLB or kube-vip"},"267":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/deployment/self-hosted/networking-6","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/deployment/self-hosted/networking","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/deployment/self-hosted/networking#external-reverse-proxy-nat-or-vpn","content":"External reverse proxy, NAT or VPN"},"268":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/deployment/self-hosted/networking-7","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/deployment/self-hosted/networking","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/deployment/self-hosted/networking#what-if-you-need-three-gateways","content":"What if you need three Gateways?"},"269":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/deployment/self-hosted/networking-8","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/deployment/self-hosted/networking","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/deployment/self-hosted/networking#decision-guide","content":"Decision guide"},"270":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/deployment/self-hosted/networking-9","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/deployment/self-hosted/networking","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/deployment/self-hosted/networking#egress-proxy","content":"Egress proxy"},"271":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/deployment/self-hosted/networking-10","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/deployment/self-hosted/networking","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/deployment/self-hosted/networking#verify-the-traffic-path","content":"Verify the traffic path"},"272":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/deployment/self-hosted/networking-11","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/deployment/self-hosted/networking","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/deployment/self-hosted/networking#expose-the-lamassu-gateway","content":"The Lamassu chart creates one shared Gateway with HTTP and HTTPS listeners. Envoy Gateway normally creates a dedicated proxy deployment and a `LoadBalancer` Service for it."},"273":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/deployment/self-hosted/networking-12","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/deployment/self-hosted/networking","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/deployment/self-hosted/networking#expose-the-lamassu-gateway","content":"External reachability is the result of the whole path. A `Gateway` resource alone does not configure your router, firewall, DNS, cloud load balancer or upstream NAT."},"274":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/deployment/self-hosted/networking-13","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/deployment/self-hosted/networking","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/deployment/self-hosted/networking#do-you-need-gatewayaddresses","content":"Usually, no. If you omit it, the Gateway controller and the cluster load-balancer implementation can assign an address and report it in `Gateway.status.addresses` and the generated Service status."},"275":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/deployment/self-hosted/networking-14","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/deployment/self-hosted/networking","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/deployment/self-hosted/networking#do-you-need-gatewayaddresses","content":"Set it only when:"},"276":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/deployment/self-hosted/networking-15","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/deployment/self-hosted/networking","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/deployment/self-hosted/networking#do-you-need-gatewayaddresses","content":"your cloud or bare-metal load balancer supports requesting a specific address"},"277":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/deployment/self-hosted/networking-16","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/deployment/self-hosted/networking","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/deployment/self-hosted/networking#do-you-need-gatewayaddresses","content":"that address is allocated to this Gateway"},"278":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/deployment/self-hosted/networking-17","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/deployment/self-hosted/networking","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/deployment/self-hosted/networking#do-you-need-gatewayaddresses","content":"the surrounding network already routes traffic for it to the cluster"},"279":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/deployment/self-hosted/networking-18","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/deployment/self-hosted/networking","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/deployment/self-hosted/networking#do-you-need-gatewayaddresses","content":"This requests `192.168.1.50`; it does not claim the IP on your LAN or make it reachable."},"280":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/deployment/self-hosted/networking-19","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/deployment/self-hosted/networking","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/deployment/self-hosted/networking#do-you-need-gatewayaddresses","content":"Keep these two settings separate:"},"281":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/deployment/self-hosted/networking-20","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/deployment/self-hosted/networking","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/deployment/self-hosted/networking#do-you-need-gatewayaddresses","content":"`gateway.addresses` requests an address for the Gateway."},"282":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/deployment/self-hosted/networking-21","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/deployment/self-hosted/networking","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/deployment/self-hosted/networking#do-you-need-gatewayaddresses","content":"`tls.certManagerOptions.certSpec.addresses` adds IP subject alternative names to the TLS certificate."},"283":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/deployment/self-hosted/networking-22","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/deployment/self-hosted/networking","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/deployment/self-hosted/networking#do-you-need-gatewayaddresses","content":"If users connect by DNS name, put that name in `tls.certManagerOptions.certSpec.hostnames`. Do not copy an upstream proxy's public IP into `gateway.addresses`."},"284":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/deployment/self-hosted/networking-23","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/deployment/self-hosted/networking","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/deployment/self-hosted/networking#recommended-single-node-design","content":"For a small VM running K3s or MicroK8s, use one external Lamassu Gateway and route every Lamassu endpoint through it:"},"285":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/deployment/self-hosted/networking-24","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/deployment/self-hosted/networking","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/deployment/self-hosted/networking#recommended-single-node-design","content":"This design uses one IP, one TLS entry point and one pair of ports. The chart already creates the required routes."},"286":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/deployment/self-hosted/networking-25","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/deployment/self-hosted/networking","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/deployment/self-hosted/networking#k3s","content":"K3s ServiceLB implements each `LoadBalancer` Service with pods that reserve the Service ports on the node. On a single node, only one Service can therefore own port 80 and one can own port 443. The default K3s Traefik Service may already hold both ports."},"287":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/deployment/self-hosted/networking-26","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/deployment/self-hosted/networking","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/deployment/self-hosted/networking#k3s","content":"For the recommended design:"},"288":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/deployment/self-hosted/networking-27","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/deployment/self-hosted/networking","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/deployment/self-hosted/networking#k3s","content":"Use only one externally exposed Lamassu Gateway."},"289":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/deployment/self-hosted/networking-28","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/deployment/self-hosted/networking","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/deployment/self-hosted/networking#k3s","content":"Ensure ports 80 and 443 are free. Disable or reconfigure Traefik if it is not part of your traffic path."},"290":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/deployment/self-hosted/networking-29","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/deployment/self-hosted/networking","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/deployment/self-hosted/networking#k3s","content":"Allow those ports through the VM firewall and any upstream security group."},"291":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/deployment/self-hosted/networking-30","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/deployment/self-hosted/networking","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/deployment/self-hosted/networking#k3s","content":"Point DNS at the VM's reachable address."},"292":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/deployment/self-hosted/networking-31","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/deployment/self-hosted/networking","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/deployment/self-hosted/networking#k3s","content":"See the K3s ServiceLB documentation for its host-port behavior and how to replace it with another load-balancer implementation."},"293":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/deployment/self-hosted/networking-32","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/deployment/self-hosted/networking","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/deployment/self-hosted/networking#bare-metal-with-metallb-or-kube-vip","content":"Allocate a VIP from an address pool reachable on your LAN. You may request that VIP with `gateway.addresses` if the selected implementation supports it. Confirm the assigned address in status rather than assuming the request succeeded."},"294":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/deployment/self-hosted/networking-33","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/deployment/self-hosted/networking","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/deployment/self-hosted/networking#external-reverse-proxy-nat-or-vpn","content":"An external public address can forward TCP 80 and 443 to the VM or to a Kubernetes-side VIP:"},"295":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/deployment/self-hosted/networking-34","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/deployment/self-hosted/networking","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/deployment/self-hosted/networking#external-reverse-proxy-nat-or-vpn","content":"The public IP belongs to the external device. Leave `gateway.addresses` unset or set it to the actual Kubernetes-side address, never to an address that the cluster cannot bind."},"296":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/deployment/self-hosted/networking-35","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/deployment/self-hosted/networking","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/deployment/self-hosted/networking#what-if-you-need-three-gateways","content":"First decide whether you need three independent data planes or only three hostnames."},"297":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/deployment/self-hosted/networking-36","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/deployment/self-hosted/networking","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/deployment/self-hosted/networking#what-if-you-need-three-gateways","content":"Requirement"},"298":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/deployment/self-hosted/networking-37","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/deployment/self-hosted/networking","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/deployment/self-hosted/networking#what-if-you-need-three-gateways","content":"Recommended design"},"299":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/deployment/self-hosted/networking-38","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/deployment/self-hosted/networking","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/deployment/self-hosted/networking#what-if-you-need-three-gateways","content":"Consequence"},"300":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/deployment/self-hosted/networking-39","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/deployment/self-hosted/networking","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/deployment/self-hosted/networking#what-if-you-need-three-gateways","content":"Several Lamassu URLs or services"},"301":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/deployment/self-hosted/networking-40","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/deployment/self-hosted/networking","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/deployment/self-hosted/networking#what-if-you-need-three-gateways","content":"One Gateway with multiple routes"},"302":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/deployment/self-hosted/networking-41","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/deployment/self-hosted/networking","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/deployment/self-hosted/networking#what-if-you-need-three-gateways","content":"One IP and one proxy fleet; this is the chart default"},"303":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/deployment/self-hosted/networking-42","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/deployment/self-hosted/networking","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/deployment/self-hosted/networking#what-if-you-need-three-gateways","content":"Independent Gateways and separate external IPs"},"304":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/deployment/self-hosted/networking-43","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/deployment/self-hosted/networking","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/deployment/self-hosted/networking#what-if-you-need-three-gateways","content":"One VIP per Gateway"},"305":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/deployment/self-hosted/networking-44","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/deployment/self-hosted/networking","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/deployment/self-hosted/networking#what-if-you-need-three-gateways","content":"All Gateways can use 80/443; requires a load balancer with an address pool"},"306":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/deployment/self-hosted/networking-45","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/deployment/self-hosted/networking","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/deployment/self-hosted/networking#what-if-you-need-three-gateways","content":"Independent Gateways on one node and one IP"},"307":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/deployment/self-hosted/networking-46","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/deployment/self-hosted/networking","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/deployment/self-hosted/networking#what-if-you-need-three-gateways","content":"Use different external ports"},"308":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/deployment/self-hosted/networking-47","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/deployment/self-hosted/networking","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/deployment/self-hosted/networking#what-if-you-need-three-gateways","content":"Clients must include non-standard ports"},"309":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/deployment/self-hosted/networking-48","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/deployment/self-hosted/networking","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/deployment/self-hosted/networking#what-if-you-need-three-gateways","content":"Separate TLS/mTLS termination behind one IP"},"310":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/deployment/self-hosted/networking-49","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/deployment/self-hosted/networking","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/deployment/self-hosted/networking#what-if-you-need-three-gateways","content":"Front-door SNI routing to internal Gateways"},"311":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/deployment/self-hosted/networking-50","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/deployment/self-hosted/networking","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/deployment/self-hosted/networking#what-if-you-need-three-gateways","content":"Advanced design; the front door uses TLS passthrough and each internal Gateway terminates its own TLS"},"312":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/deployment/self-hosted/networking-51","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/deployment/self-hosted/networking","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/deployment/self-hosted/networking#what-if-you-need-three-gateways","content":"Separate Gateway resources but shared proxy infrastructure"},"313":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/deployment/self-hosted/networking-52","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/deployment/self-hosted/networking","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/deployment/self-hosted/networking#what-if-you-need-three-gateways","content":"Envoy merged-Gateway mode"},"314":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/deployment/self-hosted/networking-53","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/deployment/self-hosted/networking","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/deployment/self-hosted/networking#what-if-you-need-three-gateways","content":"Logical separation only; listeners must have unique port, protocol and hostname tuples"},"315":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/deployment/self-hosted/networking-54","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/deployment/self-hosted/networking","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/deployment/self-hosted/networking#what-if-you-need-three-gateways","content":"Three independent `LoadBalancer` Services cannot all reserve the same node ports 80 and 443 through K3s ServiceLB. Use one shared Gateway, allocate distinct VIPs with another load-balancer implementation, or use different ports."},"316":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/deployment/self-hosted/networking-55","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/deployment/self-hosted/networking","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/deployment/self-hosted/networking#what-if-you-need-three-gateways","content":"Envoy Gateway normally provisions a proxy fleet per `Gateway`. Its merged-Gateway mode can share one fleet and address, but it is not a drop-in switch for multiple Lamassu releases: the generated Lamassu listeners use the same ports and protocols without distinct hostnames, so they conflict unless you deliberately customize the listener design."},"317":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/deployment/self-hosted/networking-56","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/deployment/self-hosted/networking","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/deployment/self-hosted/networking#what-if-you-need-three-gateways","content":"Use a front-door SNI design only when the internal Gateways must retain independent TLS or mTLS policy:"},"318":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/deployment/self-hosted/networking-57","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/deployment/self-hosted/networking","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/deployment/self-hosted/networking#what-if-you-need-three-gateways","content":"This requires distinct SNI hostnames and cluster networking outside the Lamassu chart."},"319":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/deployment/self-hosted/networking-58","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/deployment/self-hosted/networking","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/deployment/self-hosted/networking#decision-guide","content":"If one Gateway can own TLS and routing, use the chart default."},"320":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/deployment/self-hosted/networking-59","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/deployment/self-hosted/networking","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/deployment/self-hosted/networking#decision-guide","content":"If Gateways need independent policy and you can allocate IPs, use one VIP per Gateway."},"321":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/deployment/self-hosted/networking-60","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/deployment/self-hosted/networking","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/deployment/self-hosted/networking#decision-guide","content":"If only the Kubernetes resources need separation, evaluate merged-Gateway mode and make every listener tuple unique."},"322":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/deployment/self-hosted/networking-61","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/deployment/self-hosted/networking","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/deployment/self-hosted/networking#decision-guide","content":"If data planes and TLS termination must stay independent behind one IP, add a front-door SNI passthrough layer."},"323":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/deployment/self-hosted/networking-62","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/deployment/self-hosted/networking","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/deployment/self-hosted/networking#decision-guide","content":"If none of those are possible, use different external ports or change the external network design."},"324":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/deployment/self-hosted/networking-63","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/deployment/self-hosted/networking","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/deployment/self-hosted/networking#egress-proxy","content":"Internal Lamassu clients — the Vault engine connection, service-to-service calls and webhook deliveries — honor the `HTTP_PROXY`, `HTTPS_PROXY` and `NO_PROXY` environment variables. The exception is the authorization-engine connector: it uses its own transport and does not consult these proxy variables. If your deployment routes egress through a proxy, list in-cluster service names in `NO_PROXY` (for example `.svc,.cluster.local`) so internal traffic stays inside the cluster. Loopback traffic is never sent through a proxy."},"325":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/deployment/self-hosted/networking-64","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/deployment/self-hosted/networking","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/deployment/self-hosted/networking#egress-proxy","content":"The default transport of these clients bounds the dial timeout (30 seconds), the TLS handshake (10 seconds) and idle connection reuse (90 seconds) so an unreachable dependency fails fast instead of hanging; these values are Go transport defaults, not Lamassu settings. HTTP/2 is negotiated when the peer supports it. The authorization-engine connector keeps its own transport without these dial and handshake timeouts; only its overall 30-second request timeout bounds each call."},"326":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/deployment/self-hosted/networking-65","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/deployment/self-hosted/networking","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/deployment/self-hosted/networking#verify-the-traffic-path","content":"Check, in order:"},"327":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/deployment/self-hosted/networking-66","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/deployment/self-hosted/networking","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/deployment/self-hosted/networking#verify-the-traffic-path","content":"`Gateway` has `Accepted=True` and `Programmed=True`."},"328":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/deployment/self-hosted/networking-67","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/deployment/self-hosted/networking","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/deployment/self-hosted/networking#verify-the-traffic-path","content":"Its status contains the expected address."},"329":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/deployment/self-hosted/networking-68","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/deployment/self-hosted/networking","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/deployment/self-hosted/networking#verify-the-traffic-path","content":"The generated `LoadBalancer` Service has a usable external address."},"330":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/deployment/self-hosted/networking-69","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/deployment/self-hosted/networking","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/deployment/self-hosted/networking#verify-the-traffic-path","content":"Port 443 reaches that address from the client network."},"331":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/deployment/self-hosted/networking-70","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/deployment/self-hosted/networking","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/deployment/self-hosted/networking#verify-the-traffic-path","content":"DNS resolves to the externally reachable endpoint."},"332":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/deployment/self-hosted/networking-71","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/deployment/self-hosted/networking","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/deployment/self-hosted/networking#verify-the-traffic-path","content":"The certificate contains the DNS name or IP used by the client."},"333":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/deployment/self-hosted/networking-72","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/deployment/self-hosted/networking","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/deployment/self-hosted/networking#verify-the-traffic-path","content":"The Gateway API treats addresses as desired state that a controller may assign or reject; see the Gateway API overview for the resource model."},"334":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/deployment/self-hosted/overview","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/deployment/self-hosted/overview","type":"page","content":"Kubernetes self-managed","breadcrumbs":["Docs","Deployment","Kubernetes self-managed"],"tags":[],"url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/deployment/self-hosted/overview"},"335":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/deployment/self-hosted/overview-0","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/deployment/self-hosted/overview","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/deployment/self-hosted/overview","content":"Choose an installation workflow and network architecture for Lamassu on your Kubernetes cluster."},"336":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/deployment/self-hosted/overview-1","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/deployment/self-hosted/overview","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/deployment/self-hosted/overview#self-managed-kubernetes-deployment","content":"Self-managed Kubernetes deployment"},"337":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/deployment/self-hosted/overview-2","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/deployment/self-hosted/overview","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/deployment/sel