tifact_alias`"},"2823":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/data-model-42","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/data-model","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/data-model#hawkbit-mode-tables","content":"Read when resolving an artifact ID, but nothing writes it any more"},"2824":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/data-model-43","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/data-model","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/data-model#hawkbit-mode-tables","content":"`hawkbit_sw_descriptor_v2`"},"2825":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/data-model-44","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/data-model","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/data-model#hawkbit-mode-tables","content":"sw-descriptions, launch preconditions and rollout flags (a general key-value text store, keyed by instance, kind and ID)"},"2826":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/data-model-45","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/data-model","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/data-model#hawkbit-mode-tables","content":"`hawkbit_set_manifest_v2`"},"2827":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/data-model-46","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/data-model","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/data-model#hawkbit-mode-tables","content":"Signed manifests of built sets"},"2828":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/data-model-47","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/data-model","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/data-model#hawkbit-mode-tables","content":"`hawkbit_cancelled_rollout_v2`"},"2829":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/data-model-48","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/data-model","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/data-model#hawkbit-mode-tables","content":"Rollouts cancelled through this service"},"2830":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/data-model-49","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/data-model","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/data-model#hawkbit-mode-tables","content":"`latest_distribution_set_version`"},"2831":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/data-model-50","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/data-model","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/data-model#hawkbit-mode-tables","content":"Declared latest versions (shared with native mode)"},"2832":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/data-model-51","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/data-model","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/data-model#hawkbit-mode-tables","content":"Rows keyed by a hawkBit ID carry an `instance_id`, a marker of the hawkBit data they describe. If hawkBit loses its data and starts again, IDs repeat, and the service stops reading rows written for the old instance. The service re-checks the marker every 30 seconds."},"2833":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/data-model-52","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/data-model","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/data-model#hawkbit-mode-tables","content":"hawkBit keeps its own schema in its own `hawkbit` database. In the Docker Compose stack, `init.sql` creates both databases when the Postgres container first starts."},"2834":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/data-model-53","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/data-model","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/data-model#entity-relationship-diagrams","content":"The native-mode tables, with their main columns. `*_id` columns that point at another table are drawn as the relationship lines. These are logical references: the service creates no database foreign-key constraints, and `FK` only marks which column holds the reference."},"2835":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/data-model-54","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/data-model","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/data-model#launches-and-devices","content":"Values worth knowing:"},"2836":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/data-model-55","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/data-model","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/data-model#launches-and-devices","content":"`distribution_set.status` is `draft`, `built` or `build_failed`. `packaging` is `swu` or `non-swu`. `encryption_mode` is empty, `shared` or `per-device`."},"2837":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/data-model-56","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/data-model","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/data-model#launches-and-devices","content":"`launchtrack.status` is `running`, `paused`, `cancelled` or `completed`. A new launch is stored with an empty status, which means running. `aborted` is true for a cancelled launch (operator or error threshold) and stops every rollout path. The precondition outcome of the launch (`forced_preconditions`, `precondition_failures`) is stored on the row, but not the preconditions themselves: those live on the pack."},"2838":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/data-model-57","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/data-model","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/data-model#launches-and-devices","content":"`rollout_type` is not validated: only the value `percentage` makes `rollout_value` a percentage, and any other value (the dashboard sends `numeric`, the examples use `fixed`) makes it a device count."},"2839":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/data-model-58","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/data-model","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/data-model#launches-and-devices","content":"`launch_device_assignments.status` is `pending`, `active`, `completed` or `failed`. (`cancelled` also exists as a value, but only hawkBit mode reports it, for a canary whose launch was cancelled; it is never stored.)"},"2840":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/data-model-59","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/data-model","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/data-model#launches-and-devices","content":"`device_distribution_set_update.status` is `pending`, `running`, `success` or `failed` (hawkBit mode can also report `cancelled`), and its `source` is `service`."},"2841":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/data-model-60","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/data-model","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/data-model#launches-and-devices","content":"`distribution_set_module` is unique by pack, pack version, type and name. A standalone catalog module has an empty `distribution_set_id`, and its `distribution_set_version` equals its own `version`."},"2842":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/data-model-61","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/data-model","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/data-model#launches-and-devices","content":"`distribution_set_version` is unique by pack and version, and `distribution_set_artifact` by pack, version and artifact."},"2843":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/data-model-62","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/data-model","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/data-model#launches-and-devices","content":"Not drawn: `updates_schema_migrations`, a marker table the start-up data migrations use, and the hawkBit-mode tables listed above."},"2844":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/data-model-63","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/data-model","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/data-model#reading-the-diagram","content":"A **pack** (`distribution_set`) is one row that moves through versions. Each built version is snapshotted into `distribution_set_version`, with its signed manifest."},"2845":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/data-model-64","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/data-model","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/data-model#reading-the-diagram","content":"**Modules** and **artifacts** are separate: an artifact is a file in the global catalog, and `distribution_set_artifact` links it to a pack version (and optionally to one module). A module whose `distribution_set_id` is empty is a catalog module that no pack holds yet."},"2846":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/data-model-65","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/data-model","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/data-model#reading-the-diagram","content":"A **launch** (`launchtrack`) targets a group through one assignment row per device. The assignment moves `pending` → `active` → `completed` or `failed`, and `batch_index` records which batch dispatched it."},"2847":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/data-model-66","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/data-model","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/data-model#reading-the-diagram","content":"Two device tables answer different questions. `device_distribution_set_version` is what a device carries **now**. `device_distribution_set_update` is the **history** of attempts, with `version_from` and `version_to`."},"2848":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/data-model-67","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/data-model","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/data-model#reading-the-diagram","content":"`latest_distribution_set_version` is the version an operator declared devices of a group should be on, used for drift and compliance."},"2849":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/data-model-68","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/data-model","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/data-model#schema-creation-and-migrations","content":"There are no migration files. In native mode the service creates and upgrades its own schema when it starts, holding a Postgres lock so that replicas starting together do not race. It runs these steps in order (hawkBit mode only creates its six tables):"},"2850":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/data-model-69","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/data-model","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/data-model#schema-creation-and-migrations","content":"**Rename step** (`MigrateDistributionSetNaming`). Databases created before the \"update pack\" → \"distribution set\" rename have their tables and columns renamed. It runs before step 2 so that the new tables are not created empty beside the old ones."},"2851":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/data-model-70","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/data-model","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/data-model#schema-creation-and-migrations","content":"**Create and add** (GORM `AutoMigrate`). Missing tables and columns are created. It never drops or renames anything."},"2852":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/data-model-71","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/data-model","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/data-model#schema-creation-and-migrations","content":"**Data migrations.** Standalone modules (`software_module_definition` rows move into the module and artifact tables, keeping IDs and files, and the old table is dropped), device assignments (rebuilt from the legacy launch columns), and approval-threshold semantics."},"2853":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/data-model-72","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/data-model","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/data-model#schema-creation-and-migrations","content":"Most steps check the current schema instead of a version number, and the approval-threshold migration records a row in `updates_schema_migrations` so it runs only once. Repeated starts are safe, and a new database has nothing to migrate. After the schema steps the service also copies binaries from the legacy pack-scoped layout on disk into the artifact store, skipping any that are already there."},"2854":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/data-model-73","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/data-model","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/data-model#schema-creation-and-migrations","content":"`init.sql` is a Docker Compose seed: it creates the `updates` and `hawkbit` databases and still contains older table definitions, so do not use it to define the schema yourself."},"2855":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/data-model-74","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/data-model","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/data-model#schema-creation-and-migrations","content":"See Operations for what to do before upgrading."},"2856":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/data-model-75","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/data-model","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/data-model#next-steps","content":"<Card title=\"Configuration\" description=\"Blob stores, storage and every config field.\" href=\"/docs/platform/updates/reference/configuration\" />"},"2857":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/data-model-76","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/data-model","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/data-model#next-steps","content":"<Card title=\"Operations\" description=\"Back up, scale and upgrade the database.\" href=\"/docs/platform/updates/operations\" />"},"2858":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/flows","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/flows","type":"page","content":"Flows","breadcrumbs":["Docs","Platform","[Enterprise] Updates","Concepts"],"tags":[],"url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/flows"},"2859":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/flows-0","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/flows","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/flows","content":"Sequence diagrams of the important operations, for the native and hawkBit backends."},"2860":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/flows-1","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/flows","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/flows#native-mode","content":"Native mode"},"2861":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/flows-2","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/flows","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/flows#1-publish-and-build-a-pack","content":"1\\. Publish and build a pack"},"2862":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/flows-3","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/flows","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/flows#2-create-a-launch","content":"2\\. Create a launch"},"2863":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/flows-4","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/flows","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/flows#3-roll-out-a-batch-and-update-a-device","content":"3\\. Roll out a batch and update a device"},"2864":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/flows-5","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/flows","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/flows#4-react-to-a-device-finishing","content":"4\\. React to a device finishing"},"2865":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/flows-6","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/flows","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/flows#5-build-a-per-device-encrypted-pack","content":"5\\. Build a per-device encrypted pack"},"2866":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/flows-7","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/flows","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/flows#hawkbit-mode","content":"hawkBit mode"},"2867":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/flows-8","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/flows","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/flows#6-build-a-module-and-create-a-pack","content":"6\\. Build a module and create a pack"},"2868":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/flows-9","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/flows","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/flows#7-launch-and-device-update","content":"7\\. Launch and device update"},"2869":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/flows-10","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/flows","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/flows#next-steps","content":"Next steps"},"2870":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/flows-11","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/flows","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/flows","content":"These diagrams follow what the service does, step by step. Routes are relative to `/updates/v1`. For runnable commands see the native and hawkBit curl guides, and the API reference for every route and body."},"2871":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/flows-12","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/flows","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/flows#1-publish-and-build-a-pack","content":"Building turns the uploaded artifacts and the sw-description into one `.swu`. Nothing is signed or encrypted unless the build request asks for it."},"2872":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/flows-13","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/flows","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/flows#1-publish-and-build-a-pack","content":"Things to know about the build:"},"2873":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/flows-14","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/flows","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/flows#1-publish-and-build-a-pack","content":"The pack is created with a name, a semantic `version`, a `group_id`, a `type` and an optional `packaging`. A duplicate name in the group is a `409`."},"2874":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/flows-15","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/flows","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/flows#1-publish-and-build-a-pack","content":"Uploading an artifact (or a prebuilt deliverable) to a version that is already built is refused with `409`: create a new version first. A build or change that collides with another one on the same pack answers `409` too."},"2875":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/flows-16","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/flows","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/flows#1-publish-and-build-a-pack","content":"A file larger than `max_artifact_size_mb` (10240 MiB by default) is refused with `413`."},"2876":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/flows-17","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/flows","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/flows#1-publish-and-build-a-pack","content":"Encryption is chosen by the build body: `user` plus `encryption_key_name` is shared-key encryption, and `encryption_alg_name` alone is per-device encryption (flow 5)."},"2877":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/flows-18","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/flows","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/flows#1-publish-and-build-a-pack","content":"If the build fails, the pack becomes `build_failed`, `last_build_error` says why, and the pack stays editable. The selected artifacts replace the pack version's earlier artifact links."},"2878":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/flows-19","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/flows","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/flows#1-publish-and-build-a-pack","content":"Without signing fields the manifest is stored unsigned. If a signing key is given but no certificate, the build fails instead."},"2879":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/flows-20","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/flows","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/flows#1-publish-and-build-a-pack","content":"A `non-swu` pack is built with `POST .../package` into a `.tar.gz`, and a deliverable built elsewhere is attached with `POST .../swu/upload` or `.../package/upload`."},"2880":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/flows-21","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/flows","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/flows#2-create-a-launch","content":"Creating a launch decides who is targeted, and checks the pack is deliverable. Nothing is sent to a device yet."},"2881":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/flows-22","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/flows","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/flows#2-create-a-launch","content":"`?dry_run=true` stops after the precondition check and answers `200` with `qualifying_devices`, `precondition_failures`, `superseded_devices` and `never_seen_devices`. `force_preconditions` targets every device of the group and still records who failed. `distribution_set_name`, `workflow_type` and `rollout_type` are required, and so is a `rollout_value` above zero. `approval_threshold` and `error_threshold` must be between 0 and 100, and each violation is a `400`. A launch can also carry `auto`, `scheduled_at`, `name`, `description` and `weight` (see Concepts)."},"2882":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/flows-23","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/flows","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/flows#3-roll-out-a-batch-and-update-a-device","content":"One `rollout` call sends the next batch. The canary goes alone first, then batches of the configured size, chosen at random from the devices still pending. The device side below is the `direct` workflow, where a job starts in `INSTALL`."},"2883":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/flows-24","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/flows","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/flows#3-roll-out-a-batch-and-update-a-device","content":"With the `phased` workflow a job starts in `CREATED`, and some transitions need a person or system to confirm them in WFX. This service does not advance them. The `download-install` workflow, used by `non-swu` packs, runs `DOWNLOAD → DOWNLOADING → DOWNLOADED → INSTALL → INSTALLING → INSTALLED`."},"2884":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/flows-25","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/flows","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/flows#3-roll-out-a-batch-and-update-a-device","content":"With `auto` on, one `rollout` call starts the launch and the following batches are released by flow 4. A launch with `scheduled_at` is started by the scheduled-launch trigger on the leader replica once that time passes."},"2885":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/flows-26","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/flows","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/flows#3-roll-out-a-batch-and-update-a-device","content":"The `rollout` call is not always a plain `200`:"},"2886":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/flows-27","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/flows","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/flows#3-roll-out-a-batch-and-update-a-device","content":"It is refused with `400` when the launch is paused, cancelled, completed or aborted, and on an `auto` launch once any batch has gone out."},"2887":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/flows-28","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/flows","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/flows#3-roll-out-a-batch-and-update-a-device","content":"It does nothing and answers `200` while `scheduled_at` is still in the future, and while the canary is still active. It returns an error if the canary failed."},"2888":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/flows-29","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/flows","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/flows#3-roll-out-a-batch-and-update-a-device","content":"If some jobs cannot be created, those devices stay `pending` and the call returns a \"partial rollout\" error (`500`)."},"2889":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/flows-30","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/flows","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/flows#4-react-to-a-device-finishing","content":"Every state change WFX reports runs the same logic. This is what makes automatic batching, the canary gate and the error threshold work."},"2890":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/flows-31","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/flows","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/flows#4-react-to-a-device-finishing","content":"On **every** event the service updates the device's update history and writes the event to the device's metadata in Lamassu. Then, only if the state is a terminal one of the workflow, it runs these checks in order, and the first one that applies decides what happens:"},"2891":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/flows-32","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/flows","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/flows#4-react-to-a-device-finishing","content":"#"},"2892":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/flows-33","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/flows","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/flows#4-react-to-a-device-finishing","content":"Check"},"2893":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/flows-34","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/flows","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/flows#4-react-to-a-device-finishing","content":"If it applies"},"2894":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/flows-35","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/flows","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/flows#4-react-to-a-device-finishing","content":"1"},"2895":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/flows-36","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/flows","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/flows#4-react-to-a-device-finishing","content":"Is the state terminal in the workflow?"},"2896":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/flows-37","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/flows","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/flows#4-react-to-a-device-finishing","content":"If not, nothing more happens"},"2897":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/flows-38","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/flows","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/flows#4-react-to-a-device-finishing","content":"2"},"2898":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/flows-39","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/flows","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/flows#4-react-to-a-device-finishing","content":"(always)"},"2899":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/flows-40","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/flows","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/flows#4-react-to-a-device-finishing","content":"Mark the device's assignment `completed` or `failed`. On success, record the installed version"},"2900":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/flows-41","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/flows","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/flows#4-react-to-a-device-finishing","content":"3"},"2901":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/flows-42","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/flows","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/flows#4-react-to-a-device-finishing","content":"Did the canary device fail?"},"2902":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/flows-43","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/flows","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/flows#4-react-to-a-device-finishing","content":"Pause the launch. Resume to retry"},"2903":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/flows-44","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/flows","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/flows#4-react-to-a-device-finishing","content":"4"},"2904":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/flows-45","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/flows","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/flows#4-react-to-a-device-finishing","content":"Is the launch paused, cancelled or completed?"},"2905":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/flows-46","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/flows","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/flows#4-react-to-a-device-finishing","content":"Stop: no further batches"},"2906":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/flows-47","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/flows","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/flows#4-react-to-a-device-finishing","content":"5"},"2907":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/flows-48","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/flows","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/flows#4-react-to-a-device-finishing","content":"Is `error_threshold` set, and have failures reached that share of all devices (rounded up)?"},"2908":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/flows-49","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/flows","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/flows#4-react-to-a-device-finishing","content":"Cancel the launch. Pending devices are not sent"},"2909":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/flows-50","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/flows","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/flows#4-react-to-a-device-finishing","content":"6"},"2910":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/flows-51","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/flows","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/flows#4-react-to-a-device-finishing","content":"Is nothing pending and nothing active?"},"2911":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/flows-52","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/flows","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/flows#4-react-to-a-device-finishing","content":"Mark the launch `completed`"},"2912":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/flows-53","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/flows","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/flows#4-react-to-a-device-finishing","content":"7"},"2913":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/flows-54","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/flows","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/flows#4-react-to-a-device-finishing","content":"Is `auto` off, or is nothing left to send?"},"2914":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/flows-55","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/flows","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/flows#4-react-to-a-device-finishing","content":"Wait for the operator's next `rollout` call, or for the devices still in flight"},"2915":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/flows-56","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/flows","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/flows#4-react-to-a-device-finishing","content":"8"},"2916":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/flows-57","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/flows","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/flows#4-react-to-a-device-finishing","content":"Did at least `approval_threshold` of this batch succeed? (0 or 100 or more means all of it)"},"2917":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/flows-58","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/flows","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/flows#4-react-to-a-device-finishing","content":"Dispatch the next batch. Otherwise wait for more results"},"2918":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/flows-59","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/flows","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/flows#4-react-to-a-device-finishing","content":"Only devices dispatched in the current batch count toward its approval: a straggler from an earlier batch never does. The checks move the launch between these states:"},"2919":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/flows-60","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/flows","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/flows#4-react-to-a-device-finishing","content":"A new launch is stored with an empty status, which means `running`. Resuming after a failed canary re-queues the canary so it is tried again. Cancelling stops further batches but does not recall jobs that are already running on devices."},"2920":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/flows-61","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/flows","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/flows#5-build-a-per-device-encrypted-pack","content":"Each device gets its own package, encrypted with its own key. The build first resolves every device's key, then builds. A device without a key is skipped, and a launch on a pack with skipped devices is refused."},"2921":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/flows-62","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/flows","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/flows#5-build-a-per-device-encrypted-pack","content":"`uncovered_devices` lists devices without a key and also devices whose own build failed. A build where no device got a package leaves the pack `build_failed`."},"2922":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/flows-63","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/flows","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/flows#6-build-a-module-and-create-a-pack","content":"hawkBit itself has no notion of a built module, and this service links only built modules into a hawkBit distribution set. A set is never built directly: `POST .../swu` and `.../package` answer `501` in this mode. The module is built first, in the catalog, and the pack is created from it. The diagram shows the `swu-build` intent."},"2923":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/flows-64","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/flows","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/flows#6-build-a-module-and-create-a-pack","content":"The other delivery intents skip steps: `swu-prebuilt` only uploads the finished `.swu`, which is what builds the module, and `raw` only encrypts or signs the files, with no swugenerator and no sw-description (signing adds a `.sha256` checksum document and its detached signature as extra artifacts). A build can sign through the KMS and encrypt with a shared SymKMS key. Per-device encryption is refused in hawkBit mode. A linked module is frozen: to change it, edit and build it in the catalog, then link it again."},"2924":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/flows-65","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/flows","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/flows#7-launch-and-device-update","content":"The device talks to hawkBit, not to this service. The service reads progress back from hawkBit whenever it is asked."},"2925":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/flows-66","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/flows","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/flows#7-launch-and-device-update","content":"A canary group exists only when `test_device_id` is given. hawkBit decides when a group succeeds and the next group starts, using the approval and error thresholds the service gave it. With `auto` off, hawkBit pauses after each group and the next `rollout` call releases the following one. The launch response also lists `superseded_devices` (devices whose in-flight update the new rollout replaces) and `never_seen_devices` (devices that have never polled, which can stall a group that must reach its success threshold)."},"2926":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/flows-67","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/flows","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/flows#7-launch-and-device-update","content":"The `rollout` call depends on the rollout's state:"},"2927":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/flows-68","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/flows","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/flows#7-launch-and-device-update","content":"A `ready` rollout is started, and nothing happens while its start time is in the future."},"2928":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/flows-69","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/flows","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/flows#7-launch-and-device-update","content":"A paused rollout is resumed only if it is paused between batches. An operator pause needs `resume`, and a rollout stopped by its error threshold cannot be resumed."},"2929":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/flows-70","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/flows","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/flows#7-launch-and-device-update","content":"A running manual rollout releases its next group."},"2930":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/flows-71","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/flows","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/flows#7-launch-and-device-update","content":"An `auto` rollout that is already running is refused with `400`."},"2931":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/flows-72","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/flows","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/flows#7-launch-and-device-update","content":"A second `rollout` on the same launch while one is in progress answers `409`."},"2932":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/flows-73","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/flows","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/flows#7-launch-and-device-update","content":"Device authentication is a hawkBit tenant setting. Target security tokens are off by default. See Connect a device."},"2933":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/flows-74","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/flows","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/flows#next-steps","content":"<Card title=\"Publish and roll out an update\" description=\"Run flows 1 to 4 end to end.\" href=\"/docs/platform/updates/guides/publish-and-roll-out\" />"},"2934":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/flows-75","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/flows","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/flows#next-steps","content":"<Card title=\"Data model\" description=\"The tables behind these flows.\" href=\"/docs/platform/updates/data-model\" />"},"2935":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/flows-76","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/flows","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/flows#next-steps","content":"<Card title=\"Signing and encryption\" description=\"Keys, signatures and the manifest.\" href=\"/docs/platform/updates/signing-and-encryption\" />"},"2936":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/getting-started","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/getting-started","type":"page","content":"Get started with Lamassu Updates","breadcrumbs":["Docs","Platform","[Enterprise] Updates","Get started"],"tags":[],"url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/getting-started"},"2937":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/getting-started-0","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/getting-started","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/getting-started","content":"Run Lamassu Updates and its dependencies locally with Docker Compose and check that the API answers."},"2938":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/getting-started-1","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/getting-started","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/getting-started#before-you-begin","content":"Before you begin"},"2939":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/getting-started-2","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/getting-started","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/getting-started#start-the-stack","content":"Start the stack"},"2940":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/getting-started-3","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/getting-started","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/getting-started#clone-the-repository","content":"Clone the repository"},"2941":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/getting-started-4","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/getting-started","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/getting-started#set-the-host-address","content":"Set the host address"},"2942":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/getting-started-5","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/getting-started","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/getting-started#create-the-network-and-start","content":"Create the network and start"},"2943":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/getting-started-6","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/getting-started","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/getting-started#services","content":"Services"},"2944":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/getting-started-7","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/getting-started","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/getting-started#verify-the-api","content":"Verify the API"},"2945":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/getting-started-8","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/getting-started","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/getting-started#run-without-docker","content":"Run without Docker"},"2946":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/getting-started-9","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/getting-started","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/getting-started#try-hawkbit-mode","content":"Try hawkBit mode"},"2947":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/getting-started-10","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/getting-started","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/getting-started#troubleshooting","content":"Troubleshooting"},"2948":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/getting-started-11","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/getting-started","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/getting-started#next-steps","content":"Next steps"},"2949":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/getting-started-12","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/getting-started","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/getting-started","content":"This guide starts Lamassu Updates (the OTA Update Service) with Docker Compose, in its default native mode, and checks that the API answers. It takes about ten minutes plus the image build. When it works, continue with Publish and roll out an update."},"2950":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/getting-started-13","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/getting-started","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/getting-started#before-you-begin","content":"Docker with the Compose plugin."},"2951":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/getting-started-14","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/getting-started","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/getting-started#before-you-begin","content":"A running Lamassu IoT instance that the containers can reach. The service reads device groups and their devices from its Device Manager (`dms_endpoint`), and signs with its KMS (`kms_endpoint`) only when you ask for signed builds."},"2952":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/getting-started-15","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/getting-started","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/getting-started#before-you-begin","content":"A checkout of the `ota` repository with the Lamassu `core` and `sdk` modules next to it. `go.mod` replaces `lamassuiot/core` and `lamassuiot/sdk` with local paths, and the Docker build copies them from the **parent directory** of the checkout (`context: ..` in `docker-compose.yml`), so that directory must contain both `ota/` and `lamassuiot/`."},"2953":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/getting-started-16","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/getting-started","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/getting-started#before-you-begin","content":"Access to the `ghcr.io/lamassuiot/wfx:otaq` image, which the `custom-wfx` service uses."},"2954":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/getting-started-17","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/getting-started","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/getting-started#before-you-begin","content":"Optional, for hawkBit mode: a hawkBit server. Compose builds one from `docker/hawkbit`: hawkBit 1.1.0 plus an S3 artifact plugin, tagged `lamassu/hawkbit-update-server:1.1.0-s3` locally. That image is built locally and not published."},"2955":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/getting-started-18","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/getting-started","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/getting-started#before-you-begin","content":"Optional, to run the service outside Docker: Go 1.26.2 or newer, and Python 3.8 or newer with the `swugenerator` requirements installed. The Docker image already contains the compiled binary and Python with `swugenerator`."},"2956":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/getting-started-19","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/getting-started","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/getting-started#set-the-host-address","content":"The `updates` container reaches Lamassu through `host.docker.internal`, which `docker-compose.yml` overrides with `HOST_IP`. On WSL2 the default `host.docker.internal` points at the Docker Desktop gateway, not at the WSL host, so set your own address:"},"2957":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/getting-started-20","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/getting-started","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/getting-started#set-the-host-address","content":"Then check that `dms_endpoint` and `kms_endpoint` in `config-docker.yml` point at your Lamassu API (they default to `http://host.docker.internal:8080/api/...`)."},"2958":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/getting-started-21","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/getting-started","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/getting-started#create-the-network-and-start","content":"`docker-compose.yml` attaches to an existing network named `ota-net` and refuses to start without it."},"2959":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/getting-started-22","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/getting-started","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/getting-started#services","content":"Service"},"2960":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/getting-started-23","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/getting-started","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/getting-started#services","content":"Host port"},"2961":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/getting-started-24","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/getting-started","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/getting-started#services","content":"What it is"},"2962":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/getting-started-25","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/getting-started","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/getting-started#services","content":"`updates`"},"2963":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/getting-started-26","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/getting-started","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/getting-started#services","content":"`10090`"},"2964":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/getting-started-27","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/getting-started","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/getting-started#services","content":"The Updates API, with SymKMS embedded"},"2965":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/getting-started-28","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/getting-started","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/getting-started#services","content":"`custom-wfx`"},"2966":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/getting-started-29","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/getting-started","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/getting-started#services","content":"`9080` (client), `9081` (management)"},"2967":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/getting-started-30","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/getting-started","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/getting-started#services","content":"WFX, the job server that devices poll in native mode"},"2968":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/getting-started-31","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/getting-started","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/getting-started#services","content":"`postgres`"},"2969":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/getting-started-32","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/getting-started","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/getting-started#services","content":"`5000` (container `5432`)"},"2970":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/getting-started-33","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/getting-started","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/getting-started#services","content":"Database. `init.sql` creates the `updates` and `hawkbit` databases on first start"},"2971":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/getting-started-34","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/getting-started","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/getting-started#services","content":"`swupdate-device1`"},"2972":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/getting-started-35","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/getting-started","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/getting-started#services","content":"`80`"},"2973":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/getting-started-36","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/getting-started","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/getting-started#services","content":"A sample SWUpdate device client"},"2974":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/getting-started-37","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/getting-started","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/getting-started#services","content":"`hawkbit`"},"2975":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/getting-started-38","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/getting-started","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/getting-started#services","content":"`8090`"},"2976":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/getting-started-39","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/getting-started","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/getting-started#services","content":"hawkBit server, only for hawkBit mode"},"2977":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/getting-started-40","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/getting-started","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/getting-started#services","content":"`rustfs`"},"2978":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/getting-started-41","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/getting-started","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/getting-started#services","content":"`9000` (S3), `9001` (console)"},"2979":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/getting-started-42","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/getting-started","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/getting-started#services","content":"Local S3 store, only with `--profile s3`"},"2980":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/getting-started-43","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/getting-started","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/getting-started#services","content":"`docker compose --profile s3 up -d` also starts `rustfs` and `s3-init`, which creates the encrypted bucket `ota-updates` that artifacts, builds and hawkBit's artifact storage can use. Without that profile, and with `config-docker.yml`, artifacts and builds stay on the `update_files` volume."},"2981":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/getting-started-44","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/getting-started","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/getting-started#verify-the-api","content":"The second call reports the active backend and what it supports. In native mode it looks like this (shortened):"},"2982":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/getting-started-45","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/getting-started","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/getting-started#verify-the-api","content":"`supported` has one entry for each of the 22 capabilities. See Capabilities for what each one means."},"2983":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/getting-started-46","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/getting-started","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/getting-started#run-without-docker","content":"Start the monolithic entry point with a config file. It runs the Updates API and SymKMS together."},"2984":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/getting-started-47","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/getting-started","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/getting-started#run-without-docker","content":"If `OTA_CONFIG_FILE` is not set, the service reads `/etc/lamassuiot/config.yml`."},"2985":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/getting-started-48","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/getting-started","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/getting-started#run-without-docker","content":"To build `.swu` files outside Docker, install `swugenerator` into the Python environment that the config points at (the image does the same from `swugenerator/requirements.txt`):"},"2986":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/getting-started-49","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/getting-started","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/getting-started#run-without-docker","content":"The `config.yml` at the repository root is a starting point for local development, not a ready-made file:"},"2987":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/getting-started-50","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/getting-started","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/getting-started#run-without-docker","content":"It needs Postgres (`localhost:5000`) and the WFX management API (`localhost:9081`), which `docker compose up -d postgres custom-wfx` provides."},"2988":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/getting-started-51","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/getting-started","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/getting-started#run-without-docker","content":"It contains values for one developer machine: absolute `/home/alvaro/...` paths for artifact and SymKMS storage, the signer script and `swugenerator`, and a LAN IP for the Lamassu endpoints. Edit them to paths the service user can create; the service stops at start-up if it cannot create its directories."},"2989":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/getting-started-52","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/getting-started","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/getting-started#run-without-docker","content":"It stores artifacts and build outputs in the local RustFS bucket (`docker compose --profile s3 up -d`). To use local disk instead, remove the `artifacts:` and `builds:` blocks; when they are absent, artifacts default to `{update_files_base_dir}/artifacts`."},"2990":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/getting-started-53","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/getting-started","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/getting-started#try-hawkbit-mode","content":"hawkBit mode serves the same API on top of a real hawkBit server. Start hawkBit and Postgres, wait until hawkBit answers, then start the service with the hawkBit config:"},"2991":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/getting-started-54","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/getting-started","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/getting-started#try-hawkbit-mode","content":"`config-hawkbit.yml` also contains developer-machine paths, in the SWU build settings. A service pointed at a hawkBit with no registered devices builds and launches normally, but nothing downloads the update, because in hawkBit mode devices poll hawkBit directly. Read hawkBit mode before using it."},"2992":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/getting-started-55","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/getting-started","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/getting-started#troubleshooting","content":"Symptom"},"2993":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/getting-started-56","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/getting-started","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/getting-started#troubleshooting","content":"Likely cause"},"2994":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/getting-started-57","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/getting-started","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/getting-started#troubleshooting","content":"`docker compose up` fails on the network"},"2995":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/getting-started-58","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/getting-started","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/getting-started#troubleshooting","content":"`ota-net` does not exist. Run `docker network create ota-net`"},"2996":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/getting-started-59","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/getting-started","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/getting-started#troubleshooting","content":"The `updates` container cannot reach Lamassu"},"2997":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/getting-started-60","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/getting-started","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/getting-started#troubleshooting","content":"`HOST_IP` is empty in `.env`, or `dms_endpoint` in `config-docker.yml` points at an address the container cannot reach"},"2998":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/getting-started-61","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/getting-started","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/getting-started#troubleshooting","content":"`docker compose up --build` fails while copying `lamassuiot/core`"},"2999":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/getting-started-62","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/getting-started","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/getting-started#troubleshooting","content":"The build context (the parent of `ota/`) does not contain `lamassuiot/`"},"3000":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/getting-started-63","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/getting-started","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/getting-started#troubleshooting","content":"The service exits at start-up when run on the host"},"3001":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/getting-started-64","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/getting-started","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/getting-started#troubleshooting","content":"A directory in the config (`update_files_base_dir`, `sym_keys_dir`) cannot be created, or Postgres or WFX is not reachable at the addresses in the file"},"3002":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/getting-started-65","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/getting-started","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/getting-started#troubleshooting","content":"`capabilities` answers but device groups fail with a Device Manager error"},"3003":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/getting-started-66","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/getting-started","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/getting-started#troubleshooting","content":"`dms_endpoint` is wrong. The Updates API reads every group's devices from it"},"3004":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/getting-started-67","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/getting-started","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/getting-started#next-steps","content":"<Card title=\"Publish and roll out an update\" href=\"/docs/platform/updates/guides/publish-and-roll-out\" description=\"Create a pack, build it and roll it out to a device group.\" />"},"3005":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/getting-started-68","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/getting-started","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/getting-started#next-steps","content":"<Card title=\"Connect a device\" href=\"/docs/platform/updates/guides/connect-a-device\" description=\"What a device must do to receive updates in each backend.\" />"},"3006":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/getting-started-69","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/getting-started","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/getting-started#next-steps","content":"<Card title=\"Configuration reference\" href=\"/docs/platform/updates/reference/configuration\" description=\"Every config field and its default.\" />"},"3007":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/connect-a-device","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/connect-a-device","type":"page","content":"Connect a device","breadcrumbs":["Docs","Platform","[Enterprise] Updates","Guides"],"tags":[],"url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/connect-a-device"},"3008":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/connect-a-device-0","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/connect-a-device","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/connect-a-device","content":"What a device must do to receive updates from Lamassu Updates, in native mode and in hawkBit mode."},"3009":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/connect-a-device-1","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/connect-a-device","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/connect-a-device#before-you-begin","content":"Before you begin"},"3010":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/connect-a-device-2","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/connect-a-device","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/connect-a-device#native-mode-the-device-polls-wfx","content":"Native mode: the device polls WFX"},"3011":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/connect-a-device-3","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/connect-a-device","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/connect-a-device#the-job-the-device-receives","content":"The job the device receives"},"3012":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/connect-a-device-4","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/connect-a-device","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/connect-a-device#downloading","content":"Downloading"},"3013":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/connect-a-device-5","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/connect-a-device","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/connect-a-device#the-states-the-device-reports","content":"The states the device reports"},"3014":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/connect-a-device-6","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/connect-a-device","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/connect-a-device#hawkbit-mode-the-device-polls-hawkbit","content":"hawkBit mode: the device polls hawkBit"},"3015":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/connect-a-device-7","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/connect-a-device","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/connect-a-device#make-the-device-a-hawkbit-target","content":"Make the device a hawkBit target"},"3016":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/connect-a-device-8","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/connect-a-device","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/connect-a-device#configure-swupdate","content":"Configure SWUpdate"},"3017":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/connect-a-device-9","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/connect-a-device","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/connect-a-device#point-it-at-the-right-hawkbit","content":"Point it at the right hawkBit"},"3018":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/connect-a-device-10","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/connect-a-device","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/connect-a-device#signed-and-encrypted-images","content":"Signed and encrypted images"},"3019":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/connect-a-device-11","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/connect-a-device","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/connect-a-device#verify-the-result","content":"Verify the result"},"3020":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/connect-a-device-12","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/connect-a-device","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/connect-a-device#troubleshooting","content":"Troubleshooting"},"3021":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/connect-a-device-13","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/connect-a-device","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/connect-a-device#next-steps","content":"Next steps"},"3022":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/connect-a-device-14","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/connect-a-device","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/connect-a-device","content":"This guide describes the contract between a device and Lamassu Updates, for each backend. The device software is SWUpdate: this page covers what the device must send and receive, not SWUpdate's own installation and configuration, which its documentation describes. Use it when a launch is running and no device moves."},"3023":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/connect-a-device-15","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/connect-a-device","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/connect-a-device#before-you-begin","content":"A device with SWUpdate installed, and a way to run an update client: a small agent, or SWUpdate's `suricatta` module."},"3024":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/connect-a-device-16","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/connect-a-device","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/connect-a-device#before-you-begin","content":"A device identity: one ID that is the same everywhere. It is the WFX client ID in native mode and the hawkBit controller ID in hawkBit mode, and it must equal the device's ID in the Lamassu device registry (see Device management)."},"3025":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/connect-a-device-17","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/connect-a-device","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/connect-a-device#before-you-begin","content":"The device must be a member of a Lamassu IoT device group, because a pack belongs to a group and a launch targets the group's devices. In hawkBit mode group membership is also read from the registry when `dms_endpoint` is set."},"3026":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/connect-a-device-18","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/connect-a-device","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/connect-a-device#before-you-begin","content":"Native mode only: `update_domain` must be an address the device can reach. See Configuration. In hawkBit mode devices download from hawkBit."},"3027":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/connect-a-device-19","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/connect-a-device","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/connect-a-device#native-mode-the-device-polls-wfx","content":"In native mode a launch creates one WFX job per device. The device polls WFX for jobs addressed to its ID, downloads the deliverable from the Updates API, installs it and reports each state back to WFX. Lamassu Updates reads those states from WFX to drive the launch."},"3028":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/connect-a-device-20","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/connect-a-device","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/connect-a-device#native-mode-the-device-polls-wfx","content":"The sample device in `docker-compose.yml` (`swupdate-device1`) shows the minimum configuration. It takes three variables: `DEVICE_NAME` (its ID), `WFX_URI` (the WFX **client** API, `http://custom-wfx:8080/api/wfx/v1` inside the Compose network, `localhost:9080` from the host) and `PORT`. The WFX management API on `9081` is for the service, not for devices."},"3029":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/connect-a-device-21","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/connect-a-device","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/connect-a-device#the-job-the-device-receives","content":"The job is addressed to the device (the WFX `clientId` is the device ID), names a workflow and is tagged with the launch (`lms://secure-updates/<launch id>`) and the group (`lms://dms/<group id>`). Its definition looks like this:"},"3030":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/connect-a-device-22","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/connect-a-device","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/connect-a-device#the-job-the-device-receives","content":"Field"},"3031":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/connect-a-device-23","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/connect-a-device","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/connect-a-device#the-job-the-device-receives","content":"Meaning"},"3032":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/connect-a-device-24","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/connect-a-device","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/connect-a-device#the-job-the-device-receives","content":"`type`"},"3033":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/connect-a-device-25","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/connect-a-device","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/connect-a-device#the-job-the-device-receives","content":"The pack type: `rawfile`, `firmware`, or both (`[\"rawfile\",\"firmware\"]`)"},"3034":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/connect-a-device-26","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/connect-a-device","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/connect-a-device#the-job-the-device-receives","content":"`artifacts[0].uri`"},"3035":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/connect-a-device-27","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/connect-a-device","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/connect-a-device#the-job-the-device-receives","content":"Where to download the deliverable. The service appends the device ID, so each device fetches its own file. A `.swu` for SWU packs, a `.tar.gz` for `non-swu` packs"},"3036":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/connect-a-device-28","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/connect-a-device","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/connect-a-device#the-job-the-device-receives","content":"`algorithm`, `iv`"},"3037":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/connect-a-device-29","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/connect-a-device","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/connect-a-device#the-job-the-device-receives","content":"Present only for an encrypted pack: the algorithm and, for shared-key packs, the hex IV or nonce. A per-device pack carries the algorithm but no `iv`"},"3038":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/connect-a-device-30","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/connect-a-device","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/connect-a-device#the-job-the-device-receives","content":"`signature_key_id`, `signature_algorithm`, `signature_certificate`"},"3039":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/connect-a-device-31","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/connect-a-device","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/connect-a-device#the-job-the-device-receives","content":"Present only for a signed pack"},"3040":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/connect-a-device-32","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/connect-a-device","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/connect-a-device#the-job-the-device-receives","content":"The device needs the key to decrypt, and holds it itself. For a per-device pack it is the key that SymKMS assigned to that device, and each device downloads a different file."},"3041":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/connect-a-device-33","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/connect-a-device","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/connect-a-device#downloading","content":"The download answers with the bytes, or with `302` to a short-lived signed URL when presigned downloads are enabled for the build store. Make sure the device's HTTP client follows redirects. The route also answers `HEAD` and byte-range requests (`206`), so an interrupted download can resume. The URL is fixed when the pack is built, so a device never sees a new `update_domain` until you rebuild."},"3042":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/connect-a-device-34","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/connect-a-device","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/connect-a-device#the-states-the-device-reports","content":"The device moves its job through the workflow's states, and the workflow decides who may make each move. For the `direct` workflow:"},"3043":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/connect-a-device-35","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/connect-a-device","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/connect-a-device#the-states-the-device-reports","content":"The device reports `INSTALLING`, `INSTALLED`, `ACTIVATING` and `ACTIVATED`. WFX itself makes the `INSTALLED → ACTIVATE` step. From `INSTALL`, `INSTALLING`, `ACTIVATE` and `ACTIVATING` the device can move to `TERMINATED` to report a failure; `INSTALLED` has no failure transition."},"3044":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/connect-a-device-36","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/connect-a-device","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/connect-a-device#the-states-the-device-reports","content":"Workflow"},"3045":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/connect-a-device-37","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/connect-a-device","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/connect-a-device#the-states-the-device-reports","content":"Used for"},"3046":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/connect-a-device-38","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/connect-a-device","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/connect-a-device#the-states-the-device-reports","content":"Terminal states"},"3047":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/connect-a-device-39","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/connect-a-device","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/connect-a-device#the-states-the-device-reports","content":"`wfx.workflow.dau.direct`"},"3048":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/connect-a-device-40","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/connect-a-device","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/connect-a-device#the-states-the-device-reports","content":"SWU packs, no confirmation"},"3049":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/connect-a-device-41","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/connect-a-device","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/connect-a-device#the-states-the-device-reports","content":"`ACTIVATED` (success), `TERMINATED` (failure)"},"3050":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/connect-a-device-42","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/connect-a-device","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/connect-a-device#the-states-the-device-reports","content":"`wfx.workflow.dau.phased`"},"3051":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/connect-a-device-43","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/connect-a-device","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/connect-a-device#the-states-the-device-reports","content":"SWU packs with confirmation steps (`CREATED → DOWNLOAD → ... → ACTIVATED`)"},"3052":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/connect-a-device-44","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/connect-a-device","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/connect-a-device#the-states-the-device-reports","content":"`ACTIVATED`, `TERMINATED`"},"3053":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/connect-a-device-45","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/connect-a-device","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/connect-a-device#the-states-the-device-reports","content":"`wfx.workflow.dau.download-install`"},"3054":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/connect-a-device-46","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/connect-a-device","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/connect-a-device#the-states-the-device-reports","content":"`non-swu` packs: `DOWNLOAD → ... → INSTALLED`, every move made by the device"},"3055":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/connect-a-device-47","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/connect-a-device","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/connect-a-device#the-states-the-device-reports","content":"`INSTALLED`, `TERMINATED`"},"3056":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/connect-a-device-48","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/connect-a-device","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/connect-a-device#the-states-the-device-reports","content":"`wfx.workflow.dau.simple`"},"3057":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/connect-a-device-49","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/connect-a-device","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/connect-a-device#the-states-the-device-reports","content":"Minimal `DOWNLOAD → INSTALL → INSTALLED`"},"3058":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/connect-a-device-50","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/connect-a-device","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/connect-a-device#the-states-the-device-reports","content":"`INSTALLED`, `TERMINATED`"},"3059":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/connect-a-device-51","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/connect-a-device","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/connect-a-device#the-states-the-device-reports","content":"A `phased` job has moves that WFX or an operator makes, and nothing in Lamassu Updates advances them: it stays at `CREATED` until someone confirms it through WFX (the dashboard's **Next** button does that). The launch endpoints `force-version` and `sync-to-latest` use `phased` for SWU packs unless you pass a `workflow`. The workflow files are in `wfx/workflow/dau/` of the repository. The WFX HTTP API (listing jobs, updating status) is documented by WFX."},"3060":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/connect-a-device-52","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/connect-a-device","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/connect-a-device#hawkbit-mode-the-device-polls-hawkbit","content":"In hawkBit mode devices do not poll Lamassu Updates. They poll hawkBit's DDI API, and Lamassu Updates reads the resulting action state from hawkBit."},"3061":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/connect-a-device-53","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/connect-a-device","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/connect-a-device#make-the-device-a-hawkbit-target","content":"The device needs a controller ID, and a target tagged `group:<id>` for its group. With `dms_endpoint` set, the service does this itself: when it reads a group's devices from the registry it creates the missing targets and tags them. Without `dms_endpoint` you create the targets and tags yourself. Either way the device must poll hawkBit with valid credentials."},"3062":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/connect-a-device-54","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/connect-a-device","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/connect-a-device#configure-swupdate","content":"Point the device's SWUpdate (`suricatta`) at hawkBit's URL (`hawkbit.ddi_url`, which defaults to `hawkbit.base_url`), with the tenant, the controller ID and an authentication method that your hawkBit tenant accepts. hawkBit refuses unauthenticated devices by default. With target security tokens, enable them for the tenant (`PUT /rest/v1/system/configs/authentication.targettoken.enabled` with `{\"value\":true}`) and give each device its target's `securityToken`, which it sends as `Authorization: TargetToken <token>`. The hawkBit curl guide shows every request."},"3063":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/connect-a-device-55","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/connect-a-device","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/connect-a-device#point-it-at-the-right-hawkbit","content":"The device must poll the **same hawkBit** that the service is configured for. A service pointed at a hawkBit with no targets builds and launches without error, and nothing downloads it. See Troubleshooting."},"3064":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/connect-a-device-56","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/connect-a-device","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/connect-a-device#point-it-at-the-right-hawkbit","content":"hawkBit then hands the device every artifact of its distribution set. A pack with several modules runs several independent installs."},"3065":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/connect-a-device-57","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/connect-a-device","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/connect-a-device#point-it-at-the-right-hawkbit","content":"When your gateway routes hawkBit's device artifact URLs (the path of `hawkbit.ddi_url`, `.../<tenant>/controller/v1/<controller>/softwaremodules/<id>/artifacts/<file>`) to Lamassu Updates, the service serves them only for modules assigned to or installed on that controller, and answers `404` otherwise. With presigned downloads on, it redirects to a signed URL of hawkBit's S3 bucket instead of streaming the file."},"3066":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/connect-a-device-58","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/connect-a-device","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/connect-a-device#signed-and-encrypted-images","content":"If the device verifies signatures, set its public key (`public-key-file` in SWUpdate's configuration) and sign the package with the matching key. If it decrypts, it needs the same key and algorithm the pack was built with. A mismatch is the usual reason an install fails silently after a successful download. Signing and encryption explains which key, algorithm and IV each mode uses, and what the device receives."},"3067":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/connect-a-device-59","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/connect-a-device","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/connect-a-device#verify-the-result","content":"After a launch, the device's job reaches `ACTIVATED` (or `INSTALLED` for a `non-swu` pack), the launch counters update, and the device inventory lists the pack:"},"3068":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/connect-a-device-60","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/connect-a-device","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/connect-a-device#verify-the-result","content":"See Publish and roll out an update for the rest of the checks."},"3069":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/connect-a-device-61","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/connect-a-device","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/connect-a-device#troubleshooting","content":"Symptom"},"3070":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/connect-a-device-62","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/connect-a-device","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/connect-a-device#troubleshooting","content":"Likely cause"},"3071":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/connect-a-device-63","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/connect-a-device","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/connect-a-device#troubleshooting","content":"The device never sees a job (native)"},"3072":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/connect-a-device-64","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/connect-a-device","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/connect-a-device#troubleshooting","content":"It polls the wrong WFX endpoint or uses a different ID than the group member. The WFX `clientId` must equal the device ID"},"3073":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/connect-a-device-65","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/connect-a-device","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/connect-a-device#troubleshooting","content":"The job stays at `CREATED`"},"3074":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/connect-a-device-66","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/connect-a-device","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/connect-a-device#troubleshooting","content":"The launch uses `phased`. Confirm it through WFX or the dashboard, or relaunch with `direct`"},"3075":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/connect-a-device-67","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/connect-a-device","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/connect-a-device#troubleshooting","content":"The download fails with `404`"},"3076":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/connect-a-device-68","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/connect-a-device","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/connect-a-device#troubleshooting","content":"The pack is per-device encrypted and the device has no key, or the URL names another device. Check the pack's coverage and that the URL ends with this device's ID"},"3077":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/connect-a-device-69","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/connect-a-device","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/connect-a-device#troubleshooting","content":"The download succeeds and the install fails"},"3078":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/connect-a-device-70","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/connect-a-device","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/connect-a-device#troubleshooting","content":"The signature or the key does not match what the device holds. See Signing and encryption"},"3079":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/connect-a-device-71","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/connect-a-device","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/connect-a-device#troubleshooting","content":"A `non-swu` launch looks stuck although the device finished"},"3080":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/connect-a-device-72","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/connect-a-device","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/connect-a-device#troubleshooting","content":"It was launched with `direct` or `phased`, which wait for `ACTIVATED`. Launch `non-swu` packs with `download-install`"},"3081":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/connect-a-device-73","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/connect-a-device","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/connect-a-device#troubleshooting","content":"The launch never advances (hawkBit)"},"3082":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guid