ocs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/dashboard#next-steps","content":"Next steps"},"3101":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/dashboard-14","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/dashboard","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/dashboard","content":"The Lamassu dashboard is the web interface for the Updates API. This guide follows the same update as the curl guides (native and hawkBit) through the screens. Names in bold are the labels shown in the dashboard."},"3102":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/dashboard-15","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/dashboard","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/dashboard","content":"The dashboard is a separate project (`lamassu-dashboard`). This guide describes it from its source and has no screenshots, so a label can differ in a newer version. The dashboard has no translations: its labels are in English."},"3103":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/dashboard-16","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/dashboard","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/dashboard#before-you-begin","content":"Lamassu Updates is running and the dashboard can reach it. See Connect it to the service."},"3104":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/dashboard-17","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/dashboard","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/dashboard#before-you-begin","content":"A Lamassu IoT **device group** that contains the devices to update (**Device Groups** under **IoT**). A group's members are the devices that match its criteria."},"3105":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/dashboard-18","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/dashboard","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/dashboard#before-you-begin","content":"For an SWU build with signing or encryption: a signing key in **Asymmetric Keys** or a symmetric key in **Symmetric Keys** (both under **KMS**), and, for per-device encryption, keys assigned to the devices in **Device Key Inventory** (under **IoT**)."},"3106":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/dashboard-19","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/dashboard","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/dashboard#connect-it-to-the-service","content":"The dashboard talks to the Updates API at the address in `LAMASSU_UPDATES_API`, in its `public/config.js`. In the container image it comes from the environment variable of the same name."},"3107":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/dashboard-20","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/dashboard","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/dashboard#connect-it-to-the-service","content":"The dashboard appends `/updates/v1` and `/symkms/v1` to it. A trailing `/updates/v1` is accepted and stripped."},"3108":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/dashboard-21","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/dashboard","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/dashboard#connect-it-to-the-service","content":"If it is empty, the dashboard uses `LAMASSU_API`."},"3109":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/dashboard-22","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/dashboard","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/dashboard#connect-it-to-the-service","content":"When authentication is on, every call carries the user's bearer token. The service ignores it, so put a gateway that checks it in front. See Security."},"3110":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/dashboard-23","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/dashboard","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/dashboard#connect-it-to-the-service","content":"It must point at the service instance that runs the backend you want to use. A service runs either native or hawkBit mode, never both: to use both at once you run two instances, each on its own port, and point the dashboard at one of them."},"3111":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/dashboard-24","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/dashboard","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/dashboard#connect-it-to-the-service","content":"The dashboard reads `GET /updates/v1/capabilities` once, after you sign in, and hides what the backend cannot do. That is why the same screens look different in native and hawkBit mode. What changes with the backend lists the differences. If the capabilities request fails, the dashboard assumes everything is supported and hides nothing."},"3112":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/dashboard-25","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/dashboard","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/dashboard#connect-it-to-the-service","content":"To compare both backends, the user menu has an **Updates backend** switch with the options **Auto**, **native** and **hawkbit**. It appears only in development builds, or when the dashboard container runs with `DEV_OPTIONS_ENABLED=true`. Choosing native or hawkbit overrides `LAMASSU_UPDATES_API` for that browser, shows an editable **Updates API base URL** field and reloads the page. The defaults are `http://localhost:10090` (native) and `http://localhost:10091` (hawkbit) on localhost, and `<origin>/api` and `<origin>/api/hawkbit` on any other host."},"3113":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/dashboard-26","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/dashboard","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/dashboard#where-things-are","content":"The sidebar group **OTA UPDATES MANAGER** has:"},"3114":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/dashboard-27","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/dashboard","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/dashboard#where-things-are","content":"Item"},"3115":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/dashboard-28","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/dashboard","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/dashboard#where-things-are","content":"Route"},"3116":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/dashboard-29","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/dashboard","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/dashboard#where-things-are","content":"What it is"},"3117":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/dashboard-30","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/dashboard","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/dashboard#where-things-are","content":"**Dashboard**"},"3118":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/dashboard-31","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/dashboard","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/dashboard#where-things-are","content":"`/updates/dashboard`"},"3119":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/dashboard-32","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/dashboard","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/dashboard#where-things-are","content":"Page title **OTA Dashboard**: rollout health, campaigns requiring attention, version distribution and the upcoming schedule"},"3120":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/dashboard-33","page