ides/hawkbit-curl-20","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/hawkbit-curl","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/hawkbit-curl","content":"Upload artifacts and a sw-description to the pack, then build the pack"},"3303":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/hawkbit-curl-21","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/hawkbit-curl","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/hawkbit-curl","content":"Build a **module** in the catalog first, then create the pack from it"},"3304":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/hawkbit-curl-22","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/hawkbit-curl","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/hawkbit-curl","content":"Pack after creation"},"3305":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/hawkbit-curl-23","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/hawkbit-curl","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/hawkbit-curl","content":"`draft`"},"3306":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/hawkbit-curl-24","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/hawkbit-curl","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/hawkbit-curl","content":"Already `built`"},"3307":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/hawkbit-curl-25","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/hawkbit-curl","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/hawkbit-curl","content":"Who tells the device"},"3308":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/hawkbit-curl-26","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/hawkbit-curl","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/hawkbit-curl","content":"WFX job"},"3309":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/hawkbit-curl-27","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/hawkbit-curl","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/hawkbit-curl","content":"hawkBit action, read over DDI"},"3310":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/hawkbit-curl-28","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/hawkbit-curl","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/hawkbit-curl","content":"Device reports to"},"3311":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/hawkbit-curl-29","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/hawkbit-curl","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/hawkbit-curl","content":"WFX"},"3312":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/hawkbit-curl-30","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/hawkbit-curl","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/hawkbit-curl","content":"hawkBit (DDI feedback)"},"3313":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/hawkbit-curl-31","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/hawkbit-curl","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/hawkbit-curl","content":"Next batch, with `auto` on"},"3314":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/hawkbit-curl-32","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/hawkbit-curl","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/hawkbit-curl","content":"The service, from WFX events"},"3315":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/hawkbit-curl-33","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/hawkbit-curl","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/hawkbit-curl","content":"hawkBit, from its rollout groups"},"3316":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/hawkbit-curl-34","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/hawkbit-curl","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/hawkbit-curl#before-you-begin","content":"The stack is running in hawkBit mode: this service, its Postgres, hawkBit and the Lamassu device manager."},"3317":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/hawkbit-curl-35","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/hawkbit-curl","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/hawkbit-curl#before-you-begin","content":"A device group in Lamassu with devices in it. This guide uses `fleet-a` with `dev-001` to `dev-004`."},"3318":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/hawkbit-curl-36","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/hawkbit-curl","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/hawkbit-curl#before-you-begin","content":"`curl` and `jq`."},"3319":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/hawkbit-curl-37","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/hawkbit-curl","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/hawkbit-curl#before-you-begin","content":"A SWU builder configured (`swugenerator_path`), to build a `swu-build` module. Without one, `POST .../build` on such a module answers `501`."},"3320":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/hawkbit-curl-38","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/hawkbit-curl","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/hawkbit-curl#before-you-begin","content":"`config-hawkbit.yml` in the repository serves the API on port `10090`, like the native stack, so run one backend at a time on that port. `config-hawkbit-demo.yml` serves it on `10091`, which the repository's dashboard development setup points at for the hawkBit backend. Set `API` to wherever your instance listens. Through a Lamassu gateway the API is usually `https://lamassu.example.com/api/updates/v1` and each call needs your gateway credential, for example `-H \"Authorization: Bearer $TOKEN\"`."},"3321":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/hawkbit-curl-39","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/hawkbit-curl","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/hawkbit-curl#1-check-the-backend","content":"`artifact_encryption`, `software_module_composition`, `standalone_software_modules` and `software_module_replace` appear in that list too if the build settings or hawkBit's module types are missing. See Capabilities."},"3322":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/hawkbit-curl-40","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/hawkbit-curl","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/hawkbit-curl#2-create-a-module-in-the-catalog","content":"A hawkBit distribution set can only link **built** modules, so the module comes first. `delivery_intent` says how it ships: `swu-build` builds a `.swu` from your files and a sw-description. See hawkBit mode for the other intents (`swu-prebuilt`, `raw`)."},"3323":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/hawkbit-curl-41","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/hawkbit-curl","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/hawkbit-curl#2-create-a-module-in-the-catalog","content":"`type` is `os` or `application`, and `type`, `name` and `version` are required. Without a `delivery_intent` the module is `undecided`, which accepts files but cannot be built or linked until you choose one with `PUT /softwaremodules/by-id/$MID`."},"3324":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/hawkbit-curl-42","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/hawkbit-curl","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/hawkbit-curl#3-upload-the-file-and-the-sw-description","content":"Use the same `index.html` and `sw-description` as in the native guide."},"3325":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/hawkbit-curl-43","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/hawkbit-curl","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/hawkbit-curl#3-upload-the-file-and-the-sw-description","content":"A `swu-build` module refuses a finished `.swu` as input, and a `swu-prebuilt` module takes exactly one `.swu`."},"3326":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/hawkbit-curl-44","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/hawkbit-curl","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/hawkbit-curl#4-build-the-module","content":"Building replaced the module's input files with the finished `.swu`. The build body is optional. To encrypt or sign, send `user`, `encryption_key_name`, `encryption_alg_name`, `signature_key_id`, `signature_alg_name` and `signature_certificate`, as in the signing and encryption page. A module can be built once: to change it, release a new version of the module."},"3327":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/hawkbit-curl-45","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/hawkbit-curl","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/hawkbit-curl#5-create-the-pack-from-the-built-module","content":"The pack is built from the start. Its `uri` is a hawkBit download address that devices resolve themselves. In hawkBit mode `modules` takes only `source_module_id` entries, and each module must be built and compatible with the pack's packaging. Several entries make a multi-module pack, and then `GET .../swu/download` answers `400`: download each module's deliverable with `GET .../modules/:moduleKey/artifact/download`."},"3328":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/hawkbit-curl-46","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/hawkbit-curl","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/hawkbit-curl#6-preview-the-launch-then-create-it","content":"A group's devices only exist in hawkBit once the service has registered them. The service does that whenever it lists the group's devices, which a launch, a dry run, a job listing or a compliance read all do. The canary check runs **before** that, so on the first launch of a group that has not been listed yet, a `test_device_id` fails:"},"3329":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/hawkbit-curl-47","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/hawkbit-curl","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/hawkbit-curl#6-preview-the-launch-then-create-it","content":"Run the dry run without a canary first. It registers the group's devices in hawkBit as targets and tags them `group:fleet-a`:"},"3330":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/hawkbit-curl-48","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/hawkbit-curl","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/hawkbit-curl#6-preview-the-launch-then-create-it","content":"`never_seen_devices` lists targets that have not contacted hawkBit yet. A rollout group cannot finish while its devices never poll, so check this list. `superseded_devices` lists devices that already have an update in flight: creating the launch **cancels** those actions, because hawkBit replaces a target's unfinished actions with the new one. Now create the launch with the canary:"},"3331":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/hawkbit-curl-49","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/hawkbit-curl","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/hawkbit-curl#6-preview-the-launch-then-create-it","content":"`workflow_type` has no WFX meaning here: `phased` makes a hawkBit `soft` action (the device decides when to install) and anything else a `forced` one. Define a helper to follow the launch:"},"3332":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/hawkbit-curl-50","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/hawkbit-curl","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/hawkbit-curl#6-preview-the-launch-then-create-it","content":"To start the rollout later, add `scheduled_at` (RFC 3339) to the create body. hawkBit's own scheduler then starts it, and a `rollout` call before that time leaves the schedule alone. Not run here."},"3333":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/hawkbit-curl-51","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/hawkbit-curl","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/hawkbit-curl#7-start-the-rollout","content":"The service started a hawkBit rollout: the canary in the first group and the rest after it."},"3334":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/hawkbit-curl-52","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/hawkbit-curl","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/hawkbit-curl#8-play-the-device-ddi","content":"A real device runs SWUpdate's `suricatta`, which does this itself. These are the requests it makes."},"3335":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/hawkbit-curl-53","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/hawkbit-curl","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/hawkbit-curl#8-play-the-device-ddi","content":"First, devices must authenticate. hawkBit's default is to refuse them. Enable security tokens for the tenant once, and read the target's token:"},"3336":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/hawkbit-curl-54","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/hawkbit-curl","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/hawkbit-curl#8-play-the-device-ddi","content":"This is the local setup. In a deployment where devices reach hawkBit through the Lamassu gateway, `hawkbit.ddi_url` is the gateway path (for example `https://lamassu.example.com/api/hawkbit-ddi`) and devices authenticate as the gateway requires, typically with their client certificate. See Connect a device."},"3337":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/hawkbit-curl-55","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/hawkbit-curl","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/hawkbit-curl#8-play-the-device-ddi","content":"Poll. When there is work, the answer links to a `deploymentBase`:"},"3338":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/hawkbit-curl-56","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/hawkbit-curl","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/hawkbit-curl#8-play-the-device-ddi","content":"Read the deployment and download its artifact:"},"3339":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/hawkbit-curl-57","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/hawkbit-curl","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/hawkbit-curl#8-play-the-device-ddi","content":"When the service publishes the device artifact URL (the `ddi_url` path), it serves that same route itself, for modules in the device's assigned or installed set only, and with S3 presigning enabled it answers `302` to a short-lived signed URL. A device does not need to know the difference: it follows the redirect."},"3340":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/hawkbit-curl-58","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/hawkbit-curl","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/hawkbit-curl#8-play-the-device-ddi","content":"Report progress and the result. `closed` with `finished: success` is the end:"},"3341":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/hawkbit-curl-59","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/hawkbit-curl","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/hawkbit-curl#8-play-the-device-ddi","content":"The service reads hawkBit when you ask, so the launch is up to date:"},"3342":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/hawkbit-curl-60","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/hawkbit-curl","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/hawkbit-curl#8-play-the-device-ddi","content":"To report a failure, send `\"finished\":\"failure\"` in the `closed` feedback."},"3343":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/hawkbit-curl-61","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/hawkbit-curl","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/hawkbit-curl#9-release-the-next-batches","content":"With `auto` off, hawkBit pauses after each group. Each `rollout` call releases the next one:"},"3344":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/hawkbit-curl-62","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/hawkbit-curl","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/hawkbit-curl#9-release-the-next-batches","content":"Here a hawkBit action is shown as a workflow state: a scheduled action is `CREATED`, a running one `DOWNLOADING` (hawkBit does not report finer steps), a finished one (or one that finished with a warning) `ACTIVATED`, and a failed, cancelled or cancelling one `TERMINATED`. Repeat step 8 for `dev-002` and `dev-003` (the token comes from each target), then call `rollout` once more for `dev-004`. When every action is finished:"},"3345":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/hawkbit-curl-63","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/hawkbit-curl","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/hawkbit-curl#9-release-the-next-batches","content":"hawkBit decides when a batch is finished. After the last device of a batch reports, hawkBit pauses the rollout, and for a moment its group still reads `running`. The service cannot tell that pause from one an operator made, so a `rollout` call in that window answers `400` with `rollout 1 is paused; resume it first`. Call `resume` and hawkBit releases the next batch itself:"},"3346":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/hawkbit-curl-64","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/hawkbit-curl","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/hawkbit-curl#things-that-behave-differently","content":"**Automatic rollout.** With `auto: true`, hawkBit advances the groups itself once `approval_threshold` is met. The service does not run an event consumer in this mode. The thresholds are set on every rollout group, and hawkBit evaluates both percentages **per group**, not against all devices as native does. An unset or `0` threshold becomes 100, so an unset `error_threshold` never trips. The canary group always needs 100%. They apply with `auto` off too."},"3347":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/hawkbit-curl-65","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/hawkbit-curl","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/hawkbit-curl#things-that-behave-differently","content":"**A tripped error threshold.** hawkBit then pauses the rollout, and the service reports the launch as `cancelled`. `resume` and `rollout` both answer `400` for it."},"3348":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/hawkbit-curl-66","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/hawkbit-curl","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/hawkbit-curl#things-that-behave-differently","content":"**Pause and resume.** `pause` and `resume` map to hawkBit's rollout pause and resume, but only a pause an operator made can be resumed. hawkBit already holds the rollout between groups when `auto` is off, so `pause` then answers `400` (\"Rollout can only be paused in state running but current state is paused\") and `resume` answers `400` (\"not paused; use Execute to release the next batch\"). Use `rollout` to release the next group."},"3349":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/hawkbit-curl-67","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/hawkbit-curl","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/hawkbit-curl#things-that-behave-differently","content":"**Strategy read-back.** The strategy shown for a launch is derived from the hawkBit rollout's groups, not stored. A launch created with a fixed batch of 2 for 4 devices reads back as `percentage` 50."},"3350":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/hawkbit-curl-68","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/hawkbit-curl","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/hawkbit-curl#things-that-behave-differently","content":"**Static membership.** A rollout is built from the devices of the group when the launch is created. Devices added to the group later are not picked up (`launch_device_assignment` is unsupported)."},"3351":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/hawkbit-curl-69","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/hawkbit-curl","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/hawkbit-curl#things-that-behave-differently","content":"**Not available.** Per-device encryption, custom workflows (`GET /workflows` returns an empty list), editing a running strategy, marking a launch complete, pushed job events (progress is polled), set-level prebuilt upload, and building a pack directly. `POST .../swu` answers `501`:"},"3352":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/hawkbit-curl-70","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/hawkbit-curl","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/hawkbit-curl#troubleshooting","content":"Symptom"},"3353":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/hawkbit-curl-71","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/hawkbit-curl","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/hawkbit-curl#troubleshooting","content":"Cause and fix"},"3354":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/hawkbit-curl-72","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/hawkbit-curl","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/hawkbit-curl#troubleshooting","content":"`501` building a module: no SWU builder"},"3355":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/hawkbit-curl-73","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/hawkbit-curl","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/hawkbit-curl#troubleshooting","content":"`swugenerator_path` is not configured. Configure it, or upload a prebuilt `.swu` with intent `swu-prebuilt`"},"3356":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/hawkbit-curl-74","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/hawkbit-curl","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/hawkbit-curl#troubleshooting","content":"`501` building a module: no SymKMS or no KMS endpoint"},"3357":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/hawkbit-curl-75","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/hawkbit-curl","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/hawkbit-curl#troubleshooting","content":"Encryption needs `symkms_endpoint` and signing needs `kms_endpoint`. Build without those fields, or configure them"},"3358":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/hawkbit-curl-76","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/hawkbit-curl","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/hawkbit-curl#troubleshooting","content":"`400 ... is not built` creating a pack"},"3359":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/hawkbit-curl-77","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/hawkbit-curl","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/hawkbit-curl#troubleshooting","content":"A module linked into a pack must be built first. Build it in the catalog"},"3360":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/hawkbit-curl-78","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/hawkbit-curl","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/hawkbit-curl#troubleshooting","content":"`400 ... incompatible with distribution set packaging`"},"3361":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/hawkbit-curl-79","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/hawkbit-curl","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/hawkbit-curl#troubleshooting","content":"A `raw` module cannot go into a `swu` pack, and a `swu-prebuilt` module cannot go into a `non-swu` pack"},"3362":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/hawkbit-curl-80","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/hawkbit-curl","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/hawkbit-curl#troubleshooting","content":"`400 ... frozen` changing a module"},"3363":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/hawkbit-curl-81","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/hawkbit-curl","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/hawkbit-curl#troubleshooting","content":"A module linked to a pack is frozen. Edit and build it in the catalog, then link it again"},"3364":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/hawkbit-curl-82","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/hawkbit-curl","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/hawkbit-curl#troubleshooting","content":"`400 ... already built`"},"3365":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/hawkbit-curl-83","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/hawkbit-curl","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/hawkbit-curl#troubleshooting","content":"A module is built once. Release a new version of the module"},"3366":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/hawkbit-curl-84","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/hawkbit-curl","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/hawkbit-curl#troubleshooting","content":"`409 ... being built or changed by another request`"},"3367":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/hawkbit-curl-85","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/hawkbit-curl","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/hawkbit-curl#troubleshooting","content":"Another request holds the module. Retry when it finishes"},"3368":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/hawkbit-curl-86","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/hawkbit-curl","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/hawkbit-curl#troubleshooting","content":"Creating a module answers `400` mentioning that hawkBit reserves the name and version"},"3369":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/hawkbit-curl-87","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/hawkbit-curl","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/hawkbit-curl#troubleshooting","content":"hawkBit keeps the name and version of a module that was assigned to a device, even after it is deleted. Use a new version"},"3370":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/hawkbit-curl-88","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/hawkbit-curl","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/u