(assembled `.swu`)"},"3648":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/hawkbit-mode-26","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/hawkbit-mode","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/hawkbit-mode#enable-it","content":"`swugenerator_path`"},"3649":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/hawkbit-mode-27","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/hawkbit-mode","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/hawkbit-mode#enable-it","content":"Signing with the Lamassu KMS"},"3650":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/hawkbit-mode-28","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/hawkbit-mode","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/hawkbit-mode#enable-it","content":"also `sign_script_path` and `kms_endpoint` (raw modules need only `kms_endpoint`)"},"3651":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/hawkbit-mode-29","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/hawkbit-mode","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/hawkbit-mode#enable-it","content":"Shared-key encryption"},"3652":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/hawkbit-mode-30","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/hawkbit-mode","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/hawkbit-mode#enable-it","content":"`symkms_endpoint`, plus the `symkms` block or `sym_keys_dir` so the process registers the `/symkms/v1` routes"},"3653":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/hawkbit-mode-31","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/hawkbit-mode","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/hawkbit-mode#enable-it","content":"See the configuration reference and Signing and encryption. Without these keys, `GET /updates/v1/capabilities` reports `artifact_encryption: false` and the dashboard hides the encryption selector."},"3654":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/hawkbit-mode-32","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/hawkbit-mode","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/hawkbit-mode#enable-it","content":"The API listens on `app.server.port`, and clients choose it. The dashboard reads its API URL from `LAMASSU_UPDATES_API`, so point that at the instance that runs the mode you want. If you run a native and a `hawkbit` instance side by side, give them different ports, and set each instance's `symkms_endpoint` to **its own** port: it points at the same process."},"3655":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/hawkbit-mode-33","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/hawkbit-mode","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/hawkbit-mode#run-it-locally","content":"The repository's `docker-compose.yml` starts a hawkBit (host port `8090`, backed by the `hawkbit` Postgres database) and the Postgres both services use:"},"3656":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/hawkbit-mode-34","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/hawkbit-mode","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/hawkbit-mode#run-it-locally","content":"`config-hawkbit.yml` contains values for one developer machine: absolute paths for `swugenerator_path`, `sign_script_path` and the SymKMS directories, and a LAN address for `kms_endpoint`. Edit them first, and point them at paths the service user can create. The file has no `dms_endpoint`: add the URL of your Lamassu Device Manager, or the service has no device groups to launch to."},"3657":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/hawkbit-mode-35","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/hawkbit-mode","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/hawkbit-mode#run-it-locally","content":"Check the backend:"},"3658":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/hawkbit-mode-36","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/hawkbit-mode","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/hawkbit-mode#create-and-build-a-pack","content":"A hawkBit distribution set can only link **built** software modules, so the order differs from native mode. The flow is catalog-first:"},"3659":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/hawkbit-mode-37","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/hawkbit-mode","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/hawkbit-mode#create-the-module-in-the-catalog","content":"`POST /updates/v1/softwaremodules` with its `type`, `name`, `version` and `delivery_intent`."},"3660":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/hawkbit-mode-38","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/hawkbit-mode","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/hawkbit-mode#upload-its-files","content":"`POST /updates/v1/softwaremodules/by-id/:moduleID/artifacts`. This route streams the file to hawkBit."},"3661":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/hawkbit-mode-39","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/hawkbit-mode","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/hawkbit-mode#make-it-built","content":"How depends on the delivery intent (next table)."},"3662":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/hawkbit-mode-40","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/hawkbit-mode","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/hawkbit-mode#create-the-pack-from-the-built-modules","content":"`POST /updates/v1/groups/:groupID/distribution-sets` with `modules: [{\"source_module_id\": \"<id>\"}]`. The pack is created already built."},"3663":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/hawkbit-mode-41","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/hawkbit-mode","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/hawkbit-mode#create-the-pack-from-the-built-modules","content":"`delivery_intent`"},"3664":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/pla