atest-versions","content":"Launch one device to a version. Answers `202`"},"4574":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/reference/api-554","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/reference/api","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/reference/api#version-compliance-and-latest-versions","content":"`GET`"},"4575":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/reference/api-555","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/reference/api","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/reference/api#version-compliance-and-latest-versions","content":"`/groups/:groupID/version-compliance`"},"4576":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/reference/api-556","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/reference/api","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/reference/api#version-compliance-and-latest-versions","content":"Devices not on the latest version, as `{\"group_id\", \"devices\": [...]}`"},"4577":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/reference/api-557","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/reference/api","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/reference/api#version-compliance-and-latest-versions","content":"`GET`"},"4578":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/reference/api-558","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/reference/api","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/reference/api#version-compliance-and-latest-versions","content":"`/groups/:groupID/version-status`"},"4579":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/reference/api-559","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/reference/api","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/reference/api#version-compliance-and-latest-versions","content":"The full per-device matrix, compliant and outdated, as `{\"group_id\", \"rows\": [...]}`"},"4580":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/reference/api-560","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/reference/api","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/reference/api#version-compliance-and-latest-versions","content":"`sync-to-latest` takes an optional body with `groupID` (also accepted as `?groupID=`), `distribution_set_ids` to limit the packs and `workflow`. If some devices could not be dispatched it answers `207`, or `400` when none were, with `{\"err\": \"...\", \"drift\": {...}}`."},"4581":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/reference/api-561","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/reference/api","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/reference/api#version-compliance-and-latest-versions","content":"`force-version` takes `distribution_set_id` and `version` (required), `group_id` and `workflow`. The device must be a member of the pack's group. For a `swu` pack `workflow` defaults to `phased`, and for a `non-swu` pack to `download-install`. Native mode accepts only the pack's current version unless the pack has `allow_previous_version_download`, and `sync-to-latest` has the same limit. hawkBit mode ignores `workflow` in both routes."},"4582":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/reference/api-562","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/reference/api","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/reference/api#version-compliance-and-latest-versions","content":"A drift entry has `distribution_set_id`, `distribution_set_name`, `current_version`, `latest_version`, `in_sync` and `missing`. A `version-status` row has `device_id`, `distribution_set_id`, `distribution_set_name`, `current_version`, `latest_version`, `in_sync` and, when newer than the declared one, `newest_version`."},"4583":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/reference/api-563","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/reference/api","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/reference/api#device-artifact-download-hawkbit-mode","content":"In hawkBit mode the service also serves hawkBit's device artifact URL, so a gateway can publish it on the same host as the rest of the API:"},"4584":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/reference/api-564","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/reference/api","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/reference/api#device-artifact-download-hawkbit-mode","content":"Method"},"4585":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/reference/api-565","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/reference/api","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/reference/api#device-artifact-download-hawkbit-mode","content":"Path"},"4586":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/reference/api-566","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/reference/api","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/reference/api#device-artifact-download-hawkbit-mode","content":"Description"},"4587":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/reference/api-567","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/reference/api","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/reference/api#device-artifact-download-hawkbit-mode","content":"`GET`, `HEAD`"},"4588":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/reference/api-568","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/reference/api","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/reference/api#device-artifact-download-hawkbit-mode","content":"`<prefix>/:tenant/controller/v1/:controllerId/softwaremodules/:softwareModuleId/artifacts/:filename`"},"4589":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/reference/api-569","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/reference/api","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/reference/api#device-artifact-download-hawkbit-mode","content":"A module's artifact, or its `.MD5SUM` sidecar as `text/plain`"},"4590":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/reference/api-570","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/reference/api","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/reference/api#device-artifact-download-hawkbit-mode","content":"`<prefix>` is the path of `hawkbit.ddi_url`, for example `/api/hawkbit-ddi`. The route is registered only in hawkBit mode. It answers only for modules in the device's assigned or installed set, and `404` otherwise, and `:tenant` must be the configured tenant. With presigning enabled it answers `302` like the other downloads."},"4591":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/reference/api-571","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/reference/api","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/reference/api#symkms","content":"Served at `/symkms/v1` by the same process when SymKMS is configured. It stores symmetric keys and binds them to devices. The encrypt, decrypt and MAC bodies and formats are in Signing and encryption. Errors use the same `{\"err\":\"...\"}` body."},"4592":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/reference/api-572","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/reference/api","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/reference/api#symkms","content":"Method"},"4593":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/reference/api-573","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/reference/api","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/reference/api#symkms","content":"Path"},"4594":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/reference/api-574","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/reference/api","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/reference/api#symkms","content":"Description"},"4595":{"id":"/docs/pr-p