ware_module_composition`: a pack is a composition of typed modules"},"4718":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/reference/capabilities-82","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/reference/capabilities","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/reference/capabilities#per-backend-support","content":"Yes"},"4719":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/reference/capabilities-83","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/reference/capabilities","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/reference/capabilities#per-backend-support","content":"Conditional"},"4720":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/reference/capabilities-84","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/reference/capabilities","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/reference/capabilities#per-backend-support","content":"`software_module_deliverables`: each module has its own deliverable"},"4721":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/reference/capabilities-85","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/reference/capabilities","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/reference/capabilities#per-backend-support","content":"**No**"},"4722":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/reference/capabilities-86","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/reference/capabilities","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/reference/capabilities#per-backend-support","content":"Yes"},"4723":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/reference/capabilities-87","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/reference/capabilities","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/reference/capabilities#per-backend-support","content":"`standalone_software_modules`: create a module with no pack"},"4724":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/reference/capabilities-88","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/reference/capabilities","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/reference/capabilities#per-backend-support","content":"Yes"},"4725":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/reference/capabilities-89","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/reference/capabilities","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/reference/capabilities#per-backend-support","content":"Conditional"},"4726":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/reference/capabilities-90","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/reference/capabilities","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/reference/capabilities#per-backend-support","content":"`software_module_replace`: swap a module for another version of itself"},"4727":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/reference/capabilities-91","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/reference/capabilities","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/reference/capabilities#per-backend-support","content":"**No**"},"4728":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/reference/capabilities-92","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/reference/capabilities","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/reference/capabilities#per-backend-support","content":"Conditional"},"4729":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/reference/capabilities-93","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/reference/capabilities","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/reference/capabilities#conditional-flags-in-hawkbit-mode","content":"**`artifact_encryption`** is reported unsupported only when none of `swugenerator_path`, `symkms_endpoint` and `kms_endpoint` is configured. Each build option still needs its own settings: see Signing and encryption."},"4730":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/reference/capabilities-94","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/reference/capabilities","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/reference/capabilities#conditional-flags-in-hawkbit-mode","content":"**`software_module_composition`, `standalone_software_modules` and `software_module_replace`** depend on the hawkBit server having the pre-seeded `os` and `application` module types and the `os_app` or `app` set type. The service probes this with a 5 second timeout, caches the result for about five minutes and assumes support when hawkBit is unreachable. When the probe fails, all three flags are reported unsupported together."},"4731":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/reference/capabilities-95","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/reference/capabilities","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/reference/capabilities#conditional-flags-in-hawkbit-mode","content":"**`software_module_deliverables`** is always reported supported in hawkBit mode. Building a `swu-build` module still needs a `swugenerator_path`, and without one the build answers `501`."},"4732":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/reference/capabilities-96","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/reference/capabilities","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/reference/capabilities#conditional-flags-in-hawkbit-mode","content":"**`prebuilt_deliverable`**: a hawkBit pack is never built directly. A `swu-prebuilt` catalog module accepts a finished `.swu` instead."},"4733":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/reference/capabilities-97","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/reference/capabilities","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/reference/capabilities#flags-that-differ-in-meaning","content":"Both backends report `software_module_composition`, but importing a module **links** it in hawkBit mode (both packs share one module) and **copies** it in native mode. The reusable-modules list reports this per candidate in its `shared` field, so a client can tell the operator which one they get. See Concepts."},"4734":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/reference/capabilities-98","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/reference/capabilities","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/reference/capabilities#flags-that-differ-in-meaning","content":"In native mode a launch dispatches one job per device with a single download URI, so a module has no deliverable of its own: the pack builds one `.swu` from every module's inputs. That is why `software_module_deliverables` and `software_module_replace` are unsupported there."},"4735":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/reference/capabilities-99","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/reference/capabilities","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/reference/capabilities#what-a-client-should-do","content":"Call `capabilities` once at start-up and before showing a feature the table marks as backend-dependent."},"4736":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/reference/capabilities-100","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/reference/capabilities","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/reference/capabilities#what-a-client-should-do","content":"Treat a `501` on a route as authoritative: hide the action instead of retrying."},"4737":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/reference/capabilities-101","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/reference/capabilities","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/reference/capabilities#what-a-client-should-do","content":"Do not infer the backend from the URL. Both serve the same `/updates/v1` routes; see the API reference for which routes answer `501` in which backend."},"4738":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/reference/capabilities-102","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/reference/capabilities","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/reference/capabilities#what-a-client-should-do","content":"Re-read the capabilities after changing hawkBit's module types or the build configuration."},"4739":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/reference/capabilities-103","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/reference/capabilities","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/reference/capabilities#next-steps","content":"API reference"},"4740":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/reference/capabilities-104","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/reference/capabilities","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/reference/capabilities#next-steps","content":"hawkBit mode"},"4741":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/reference/configuration","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/reference/configuration","type":"page","content":"Configuration reference","breadcrumbs":["Docs","Platform","[Enterprise] Updates","Reference"],"tags":[],"url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/reference/configuration"},"4742":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/reference/configuration-0","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/reference/configuration","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/reference/configuration","content":"Every configuration key of Lamassu Updates, its default, which backend reads it, and how to override it with environment variables."},"4743":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/reference/configuration-1","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/reference/configuration","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/reference/configuration#how-the-configuration-is-loaded","content