environment variable: the name is the key path in upper case with dots replaced by underscores. `KMS_ENDPOINT` overrides `kms_endpoint`, `STORAGE_PASSWORD` overrides `storage.password` and `BUILDS_PRESIGN_TTL` overrides `builds.presign.ttl`. The key must exist in the file (an empty value is enough): the loader only considers keys it has read from it."},"5035":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/reference/configuration-293","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/reference/configuration","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/reference/configuration#environment-variables","content":"Variables the code reads besides these overrides:"},"5036":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/reference/configuration-294","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/reference/configuration","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/reference/configuration#environment-variables","content":"Variable"},"5037":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/reference/configuration-295","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/reference/configuration","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/reference/configuration#environment-variables","content":"Description"},"5038":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/reference/configuration-296","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/reference/configuration","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/reference/configuration#environment-variables","content":"`OTA_CONFIG_FILE`"},"5039":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/reference/configuration-297","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/reference/configuration","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/reference/configuration#environment-variables","content":"Configuration file path."},"5040":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/reference/configuration-298","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/reference/configuration","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/reference/configuration#environment-variables","content":"`POD_NAME`, `POD_NAMESPACE`"},"5041":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/reference/configuration-299","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/reference/configuration","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/reference/configuration#environment-variables","content":"Identity and namespace for Kubernetes leader election. The Helm chart sets them. If unset, the hostname and the service-account namespace file are used."},"5042":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/reference/configuration-300","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/reference/configuration","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/reference/configuration#environment-variables","content":"`TMPDIR`"},"5043":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/reference/configuration-301","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/reference/configuration","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/reference/configuration#environment-variables","content":"Where uploads and builds write temporary files (Go's temporary directory)."},"5044":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/reference/configuration-302","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/reference/configuration","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/reference/configuration#environment-variables","content":"`SERVER_PORT`"},"5045":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/reference/configuration-303","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/reference/configuration","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/reference/configuration#environment-variables","content":"Used only by the health check of the Docker image to find the port. Default `10090`."},"5046":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/reference/configuration-304","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/reference/configuration","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/reference/configuration#environment-variables","content":"`AWS_*`"},"5047":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/reference/configuration-305","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/reference/configuration","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/reference/configuration#environment-variables","content":"The AWS default credential chain, when an S3 or AWS KMS block has no explicit credential."},"5048":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/reference/configuration-306","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/reference/configuration","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/reference/configuration#environment-variables","content":"For Docker Compose, the `.env` file is read by `docker-compose.yml`, not by the service: `HOST_IP`, `HAWKBIT_ADMIN_PASSWORD`, `HAWKBIT_ARTIFACT_STORAGE` and the `HAWKBIT_ARTIFACT_S3_*` and `LOCAL_S3_*` variables. See `.env.example` in the repository."},"5049":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/reference/configuration-307","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/reference/configuration","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/reference/configuration#environment-variables","content":"With `app.logs.level: debug`, the service writes the whole loaded configuration to the log at start-up, including `storage.password`, `encryption.local_key`, S3 keys and `hawkbit.password`. In `native` mode the `storage` block, password included, is also printed to standard output at every start, whatever the log level. Use `info` or higher anywhere logs are stored or shared, and keep secrets in a secret store, not in the file (see the `*_file` credentials above)."},"5050":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/reference/configuration-308","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/reference/configuration","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/reference/configuration#minimal-configurations","content":"`native` mode needs the database, the endpoints it calls and storage paths. Start from `config-docker.yml`:"},"5051":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/reference/configuration-309","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/reference/configuration","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/reference/configuration#minimal-configurations","content":"`hawkbit` mode needs `mode: hawkbit`, `hawkbit.base_url`, the Management API credentials and the `storage` block. Add the build settings only if you want builds. The keys below are the ones `config-hawkbit.yml` uses:"},"5052":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/reference/configuration-310","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/reference/configuration","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/reference/configuration#minimal-configurations","content":"In `hawkbit` mode the SymKMS routes are registered only when `symkms.storage.type` or `sym_keys_dir` is set. With `symkms_endpoint` set but neither of those, every key lookup would be answered `404` by the service itself."},"5053":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/reference/configuration-311","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/reference/configuration","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/reference/configuration#symkms-as-its-own-process","content":"The `cmd/symkms` binary runs SymKMS alone. Its configuration has only `app` (as above), `symkms` (a storage block) and `sym_keys_dir`. Its key directory defaults to `/data/symmetric_keys` when neither `symkms.storage.local_dir` nor `sym_keys_dir` is set. It serves `/symkms/v1/*` but no 