w/pr-56/platform/updates/security","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/security#summary","content":"**None in the service.** Every route is open to anyone who can reach the port. The gateway must authenticate."},"5075":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/security-16","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/security","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/security#summary","content":"Authorization"},"5076":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/security-17","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/security","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/security#summary","content":"**No roles or per-group permissions.** The service only does structural checks (see What the service checks). The gateway must authorize."},"5077":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/security-18","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/security","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/security#summary","content":"TLS and mTLS (inbound)"},"5078":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/security-19","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/security","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/security#summary","content":"**Not implemented.** The service always serves plain HTTP."},"5079":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/security-20","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/security","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/security#summary","content":"TLS to other systems"},"5080":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/security-21","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/security","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/security#summary","content":"Postgres: always `sslmode=disable`. KMS: not verified in `native` mode, and the SWU signer script uses `curl -k`. See Outbound connections."},"5081":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/security-22","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/security","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/security#summary","content":"CORS"},"5082":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/security-23","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/security","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/security#summary","content":"Any origin and any header are allowed."},"5083":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/security-24","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/security","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/security#summary","content":"Rate limiting, security headers"},"5084":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/security-25","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/security","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/security#summary","content":"None added by the service."},"5085":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/security-26","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/security","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/security#summary","content":"Package signing"},"5086":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/security-27","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/security","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/security#summary","content":"Available, through the Lamassu KMS. See Signing and encryption."},"5087":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/security-28","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/security","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/security#summary","content":"Package encryption"},"5088":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/security-29","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/security","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/security#summary","content":"Available: shared key or per-device key."},"5089":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/security-30","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/security","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/security#summary","content":"At-rest encryption"},"5090":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/security-31","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/security","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/security#summary","content":"Available for artifacts, builds and keys, through the `encryption` block of each storage block."},"5091":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/security-32","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/security","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/security#summary","content":"The `cert_file`, `key_file` and `authentication.mutual_tls.*` keys exist in the configuration structs but are not read, so setting them does nothing."},"5092":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/security-33","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/security","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/security#what-to-put-in-front-of-it","content":"Run the service behind a gateway or reverse proxy that:"},"5093":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/security-34","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/security","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/security#what-to-put-in-front-of-it","content":"**Terminates TLS** between clients and the service."},"5094":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/security-35","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/security","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/security#what-to-put-in-front-of-it","content":"**Authenticates and authorizes** callers: operators for the API, and devices for the download routes. A device must only reach its own download paths, so match the device certificate to the `:deviceID` (or `:controllerId`) in the path."},"5095":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/security-36","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/security","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/security#what-to-put-in-front-of-it","content":"**Restricts the dangerous routes** to the callers that need them (see below)."},"5096":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/security-37","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/security","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/security#what-to-put-in-front-of-it","content":"Keep the service on a private network. Devices need to reach only the download routes and, in `native` mode, the WFX **client** listener. In `hawkbit` mode they talk to hawkBit (and to the signed-URL store) and not to this service, except for the artifact download route described in hawkBit mode."},"5097":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/security-38","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/security","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/security#what-to-put-in-front-of-it","content":"WFX has a client listener (`8080` in Compose, published as `9080`) and a management listener (`8081`, published as `9081`). Lamassu Updates authenticates neither. Devices need the client listener only: do not expose the management port to devices or untrusted networks."},"5098":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/security-39","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/security","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/security#how-the-service-identifies-itself-to-others","content":"The service does not forward the caller's identity. Calls to the Lamassu Device Manager and the KMS carry the fixed header `X-Principal-ID: admin-mode`, which the platform's authorization layer accepts for internal callers and which the platform gateway strips from external traffic. The value is not configurable, so point `dms_endpoint` and `kms_endpoint` at internal service addresses, not at a public gateway path that would reject or forward it. SymKMS calls from the service carry no credential."},"5099":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/security-40","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/security","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/security#routes-to-restrict","content":"Route"},"5100":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/security-41","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/security","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/security#routes-to-restrict","content":"Why"},"5101":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/security-42","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/security","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/security#routes-to-restrict","content":"`GET /symkms/v1/:keyID/raw`"},"5102":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/security-43","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/security","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/security#routes-to-restrict","content":"Returns raw key material."},"5103":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/security-44","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/security","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/security#routes-to-restrict","content":"`GET /symkms/v1/inventory/:deviceID/key`"},"5104":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/security-45","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/security","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/security#routes-to-restrict","content":"Returns a device's raw key material. The Updates service uses it during a per-device build."},"5105":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/security-46","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/security","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/security#routes-to-restrict","content":"`POST /symkms/v1/`, `DELETE /symkms/v1/:keyID`, key assignment routes"},"5106":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/security-47","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/security","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/security#routes-to-restrict","content":"Create, delete and assign encryption keys."},"5107":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/security-48","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/security","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/security#routes-to-restrict","content":"`POST /symkms/v1/encrypt`, `/decrypt`, `/mac`"},"5108":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/security-49","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/security","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/security#routes-to-restrict","content":"Use stored keys on arbitrary data."},"5109":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/security-50","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/security","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/security#routes-to-restrict","content":"`PUT /updates/v1/jobs/:jobID/transition`"},"5110":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/security-51","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/security","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/security#routes-to-restrict","content":"Forges a job state change with no ownership check. Registered only when `enable_test_endpoints` is `true`: keep it `false`."},"5111":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/security-52","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/security","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/security#routes-to-restrict","content":"Every `POST`, `PUT` and `DELETE` of `/updates/v1`"},"5112":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/security-53","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/security","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/security#routes-to-restrict","content":"Build, launch, cancel and delete. Restrict them to operators."},"5113":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/security-54","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/security","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/security#routes-to-restrict","content":"`GET` of artifacts, descriptors and `artifacts-archive`"},"5114":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/security-55","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/security","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/security#routes-to-restrict","content":"Expose firmware sources and sw-descriptions."},"5115":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/security-56","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/security","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/security#routes-to-restrict","content":"Download routes with `:deviceID`"},"5116":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/security-57","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/security","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/security#routes-to-restrict","content":"Per-device builds are encrypted with that device's key, but the route itself checks nothing about who asks."},"5117":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/security-58","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/security","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/security#what-the-service-checks","content":"These are defence in depth, not a substitute for the gateway:"},"5118":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/security-59","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/security","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/security#what-the-service-checks","content":"A launch is addressed under its group: an operation on a launch through another group's path answers `404`, exactly as for a missing launch, and changes nothing."},"5119":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/security-60","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/security","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/security#what-the-service-checks","content":"Approval and error thresholds must be between 0 and 100."},"5120":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/security-61","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/security","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/security#what-the-service-checks","content":"In `native` mode, pack, group and device identifiers used in paths are validated so they cannot escape the storage directories, and a per-device pack never falls back to the shared build for a device."},"5121":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/security-62","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/security","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/security#what-the-service-checks","content":"An upload under a `.swu` name must really be a SWU: other content is refused with `400`."},"5122":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/security-63","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/security","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/security#what-the-service-checks","content":"An uploaded file larger than `max_artifact_size_mb` is refused with `413`."},"5123":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/security-64","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/security","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/security#what-the-service-checks","content":"In `hawkbit` mode the DDI artifact route serves a file only if the module is assigned to or installed on that device."},"5124":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/security-65","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/security","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/security#what-the-service-checks","content":"Anything that changes a built version is refused (`409`): versions are immutable."},"5125":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/security-66","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/security","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/security#presigned-download-urls","content":"With `presign.enabled`, a download is answered `302` to a short-lived URL of the S3 store. The service authorizes the caller first (the gateway for the static route and, in `hawkbit` mode, the device's assignment); the store then checks only the signature, so **the URL is a bearer capability**: whoever holds it can fetch that one object until it expires. The design keeps that acceptable:"},"5126":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/security-67","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/security","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/security#presigned-download-urls","content":"The TTL is short (default 60 s). It bounds when a GET can **start**: a transfer in progress finishes after expiry, and a device that retries or resumes goes back to the static endpoint for a fresh URL. A URL already signed for the same object is reused while it has `min_remaining` validity left (default `min(25s, ttl/2)`); it grants no more than a fresh one."},"5127":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/security-68","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/security","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/security#presigned-download-urls","content":"The signing credential must be **read-only** and different from the storage credential. At start-up the service probes with a write and refuses to run if the credential can write, is the storage's own, or is rejected by the store. A signature covers the method and the key, so a URL cannot be turned into a `PUT` or aimed at another object."},"5128":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/security-69","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/security","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/security#presigned-download-urls","content":"The signed host is the store's **public** origin (`presign.public_endpoint`), because the signature covers the `Host` header."},"5129":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/security-70","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/security","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/security#presigned-download-urls","content":"It cannot be combined with at-rest encryption of the same store (devices would receive ciphertext)."},"5130":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/security-71","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/security","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/security#presigned-download-urls","content":"Redirect responses carry `Cache-Control: no-store`. `HEAD` requests are answered by the service, not redirected. If signing fails, the service streams the file instead of failing the update."},"5131":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/security-72","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/security","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/security#presigned-download-urls","content":"Rotate the signing credential by updating the files named by `access_key_id_file` and `secret_access_key_file`: they are re-read every minute."},"5132":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/security-73","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/security","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/security#presigned-download-urls","content":"The store itself must be reachable by devices at the public endpoint, and should accept only the read-only credential on the prefix it serves. Do not publish the store's console or S3 API with default credentials."},"5133":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/security-74","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/security","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/security#outbound-connections","content":"Connection"},"5134":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/security-75","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/security","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/security#outbound-connections","content":"Transport security"},"5135":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/security-76","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/security","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/security#outbound-connections","content":"Postgres"},"5136":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/security-77","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/security","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/security#outbound-connections","content":"`sslmode=disable`, not configurable. Keep the database on a private network."},"5137":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/security-78","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/security","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/security#outbound-connections","content":"Lamassu Device Manager"},"5138":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/security-79","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/security","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/security#outbound-connections","content":"The Lamassu platform SDK client with its default settings."},"5139":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/security-80","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/security","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/security#outbound-connections","content":"Lamassu KMS"},"5140":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/security-81","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/security","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/security#outbound-connections","content":"`native` mode: certificate verification is **skipped** for the service's own calls, and the SWU signer script uses `curl -k`. `hawkbit` mode: the service's calls verify the certificate, the script still does not. Use an internal address you trust."},"5141":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/security-82","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/security","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/security#outbound-connections","content":"SymKMS"},"5142":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/security-83","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/security","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/security#outbound-connections","content":"The scheme of `symkms_endpoint` (normally the service itself, over plain HTTP in the examples), with no credential. Raw key material crosses this connection: keep it on `localhost` or a private network."},"5143":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/security-84","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/security","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/security#outbound-connections","content":"hawkBit Management API"},"5144":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/security-85","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/security","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/security#outbound-connections","content":"HTTP Basic with `hawkbit.username` and `hawkbit.password`. Use HTTPS."},"5145":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/security-86","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/security","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/security#outbound-connections","content":"WFX"},"5146":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/security-87","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/security","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/security#outbound-connections","content":"The scheme of `wfx_endpoint` (plain HTTP in the examples), to the management listener."},"5147":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/security-88","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/security","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/security#secrets","content":"`encryption.local_key`, S3 credentials and database passwords must come from a secret store, not from a file in the repository. The example configurations contain development values only. Prefer the `*_file` form of S3 and presign credentials, which the service re-reads every minute."},"5148":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/security-89","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/security","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/security#secrets","content":"The Helm chart renders all of `config` into a ConfigMap. See Operations. Override its placeholder database password."},"5149":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/security-90","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/security","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/security#secrets","content":"With `app.logs.level: debug` the service logs the whole configuration, secrets included, and in `native` mode it prints the `storage` block (with its password) to standard output at every start. Use `info` or higher in any environment whose logs are stored."},"5150":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/security-91","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/security","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/security#secrets","content":"A lost `encryption.local_key` makes everything stored with it unreadable. See Backup and restore."},"5151":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/security-92","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/security","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/security#secrets","content":"Signing keys stay in the Lamassu KMS: the service never holds the private key. Device encryption keys do live in SymKMS (optionally encrypted at rest), because packages must be encrypted with them."},"5152":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/security-93","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/security","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/security#secrets","content":"The container image does not drop privileges. Set a `securityContext` that suits your cluster."},"5153":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/security-94","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/security","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/security#hawkbit-mode","content":"The Management API user is a full administrator of hawkBit. Change the default (`admin`) credential, keep the API off the device network and serve it over HTTPS."},"5154":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/security-95","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/security","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/security#hawkbit-mode","content":"Devices authenticate to hawkBit, not to this service. hawkBit 1.1.0 has no anonymous mode: enable a target security token, a gateway token or the reverse-proxy header authenticator, and for the last restrict which addresses may set its headers. Leaving device authentication off, which is acceptable only on a throw-away test stack, lets anything that can reach hawkBit impersonate a device. See hawkBit mode."},"5155":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/security-96","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/security","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/security#hawkbit-mode","content":"hawkBit does not encrypt artifacts at rest. Enable default encryption in the bucket, or use encrypted (shared-key) packages."},"5156":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/security-97","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/security","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/security#request-limits","content":"A request body can be up to `max_artifact_size_mb` plus 1 MiB (10 GiB by default), and a request can take up to 6 hours, so large uploads work. Streamed uploads use temporary disk under `TMPDIR`. Apply tighter limits at the gateway for callers that are not trusted: there is no rate limiting in the service."},"5157":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/signing-and-encryption","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/signing-and-encryption","type":"page","content":"Signing and encryption","breadcrumbs":["Docs","Platform","[Enterprise] Updates","Concepts"],"tags":[],"url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/signing-and-encryption"},"5158":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/signing-and-encryption-0","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/signing-and-encryption","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/signing-and-encryption","content":"Sign deliverables with the Lamassu KMS, encrypt them with a shared or per-device key, and manage device keys in SymKMS."},"5159":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/signing-and-encryption-1","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/signing-and-encryption","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/signing-and-encryption#signing","content":"Signing"},"5160":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/signing-and-encryption-2","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/signing-and-encryption","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/signing-and-encryption#set-up-signing","content":"Set up signing"},"5161":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/signing-and-encryption-3","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/signing-and-encryption","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/signing-and-encryption#create-the-key-and-a-certificate","content":"Create the key and a certificate"},"5162":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/signing-and-encryption-4","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/signing-and-encryption","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/signing-and-encryption#configure-the-service","content":"Configure the service"},"5163":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/signing-and-encryption-5","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/signing-and-encryption","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/signing-and-encryption#send-the-signature-fields-in-the-build","content":"Send the signature fields in the build"},"5164":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/signing-and-encryption-6","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/signing-and-encryption","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/signing-and-encryption#signed-manifests","content":"Signed manifests"},"5165":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/signing-and-encryption-7","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/signing-and-encryption","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/signing-and-encryption#encryption-modes","content":"Encryption modes"},"5166":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/signing-and-encryption-8","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/signing-and-encryption","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/signing-and-encryption#algorithms","content":"Algorithms"},"5167":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/signing-and-encryption-9","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/signing-and-encryption","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/signing-and-encryption#set-up-per-device-encryption","content":"Set up per-device encryption"},"5168":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/signing-and-encryption-10","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/signing-and-encryption","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/signing-and-encryption#create-a-key-per-device","content":"Create a key per device"},"5169":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/signing-and-encryption-11","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/signing-and-encryption","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/signing-and-encryption#assign-it-to-the-device","content":"Assign it to the device"},"5170":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/signing-and-encryption-12","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/signing-and-encryption","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/signing-and-encryption#put-the-same-key-on-the-device","content":"Put the same key on the device"},"5171":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/signing-and-encryption-13","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/signing-and-encryption","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/signing-and-encryption#build","content":"Build"},"5172":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/signing-and-encryption-14","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/signing-and-encryption","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/signing-and-encryption#symkms","content":"SymKMS"},"5173":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/signing-and-encryption-15","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/signing-and-encryption","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/signing-and-encryption#request-bodies","content":"Request bodies"},"5174":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/signing-and-encryption-16","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/signing-and-encryption","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/signing-and-encryption","content":"This page explains how Lamassu Updates protects what it delivers: which keys sign and encrypt a package, how to configure them, and what each backend supports. There are three independent layers."},"5175":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/signing-and-encryption-17","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/signing-and-encryption","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/signing-and-encryption","content":"Layer"},"5176":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/signing-and-encryption-18","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/signing-and-encryption","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/signing-and-encryption","content":"Protects"},"5177":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/signing-and-encryption-19","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/signing-and-encryption","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/signing-and-encryption","content":"Configured in"},"5178":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/signing-and-encryption-20","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/signing-and-encryption","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/signing-and-encryption","content":"Package signing"},"5179":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/signing-and-encryption-21","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/signing-and-encryption","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/signing-and-encryption","content":"That the package came from you and is unmodified"},"5180":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/signing-and-encryption-22","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/signing-and-encryption","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/signing-and-encryption","content":"A signing key and certificate in the Lamassu KMS, plus `kms_endpoint` and `sign_script_path`"},"5181":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/signing-and-encryption-23","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/signing-and-encryption","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/signing-and-encryption","content":"Package encryption"},"5182":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/signing-and-encryption-24","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/signing-and-encryption","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/signing-and-encryption","content":"The contents of the package in transit and on the device's download path"},"5183":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/signing-and-encryption-25","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/signing-and-encryption","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/signing-and-encryption","content":"The build request, plus a key in SymKMS"},"5184":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/signing-and-encryption-26","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/signing-and-encryption","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/signing-and-encryption","content":"At-rest encryption"},"5185":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/signing-and-encryption-27","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/signing-and-encryption","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/signing-and-encryption","content":"Artifacts, builds and keys stored by the service"},"5186":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/signing-and-encryption-28","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/signing-and-encryption","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/signing-and-encryption","content":"The `encryption` block of each blob storage block"},"5187":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/signing-and-encryption-29","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/signing-and-encryption","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/signing-and-encryption#signing","content":"Signing is optional. When you ask for it, `swugenerator` calls the configured signer script (`sign_script_path`, which is `sign_kms.sh`), and the script asks the Lamassu KMS (`kms_endpoint`) to sign. The private key never reaches the machine that builds the package."},"5188":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/signing-and-encryption-30","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/signing-and-encryption","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/signing-and-encryption#signing","content":"For `.swu` builds both settings must be set: the service refuses a signing request when either is missing."},"5189":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/signing-and-encryption-31","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/signing-and-encryption","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/signing-and-encryption#signing","content":"Signing a manifest, a `non-swu` package or a hawkBit `raw` module calls the KMS directly from the service and needs only `kms_endpoint`."},"5190":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/signing-and-encryption-32","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/signing-and-encryption","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/signing-and-encryption#signing","content":"Select the key in the build request with `signature_key_id`, `signature_alg_name` (default `RSASSA_PSS_SHA_256`; `-` and `_` are interchangeable) and `signature_certificate` (PEM). The three fields go together: a request with a key but no algorithm or certificate is refused, never built unsigned."},"5191":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/signing-and-encryption-33","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/signing-and-encryption","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/signing-and-encryption#create-the-key-and-a-certificate","content":"In the Lamassu KMS, create (or choose) the signing key and issue a certificate for it from a CA your devices trust. See Keys and cryptographic engines. The key ID is your `signature_key_id`."},"5192":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/signing-and-encryption-34","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/signing-and-encryption","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/signing-and-encryption#configure-the-service","content":"Set `kms_endpoint` and `sign_script_path` (`/app/sign_kms.sh` in the image). `swugenerator` calls the script with the key ID, the KMS URL, the algorithm and the path of the certificate file, which the script requires. The script writes a debug log to `/tmp/sign_kms_debug.log`."},"5193":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/signing-and-encryption-35","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/signing-and-encryption","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/signing-and-encryption#send-the-signature-fields-in-the-build","content":"Include `signature_key_id`, `signature_alg_name` and `signature_certificate` in the build body. In `hawkbit` mode they go in the module build body."},"5194":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/signing-and-encryption-36","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/signing-and-encryption","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/signing-and-encryption#send-the-signature-fields-in-the-build","content":"SWUpdate verifies a `.swu` with a CMS `SignedData` signature, and the service requires CMS for the manifests it signs itself. A Lamassu KMS that ignores the `Accept` header and answers with a bare signature in a JSON envelope produces a signature no device can verify. Where the service signs itself (version manifests, set manifests, raw-module checksums) it refuses such an answer and the operation fails with `the KMS did not return a PKCS7/CMS signature`. The SWU signer script does not check the format: it unwraps the answer and embeds it, so against a KMS without CMS support a `.swu` build can succeed and still be rejected by a device that sets `public-key-file`. Test one signed build on a real device before you rely on a KMS version."},"5195":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/signing-and-encryption-37","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/signing-and-encryption","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/signing-and-encryption#send-the-signature-fields-in-the-build","content":"`sign_kms_nocms.sh` is a variant of the script that takes no certificate. The service's own manifest signing is separate: it always sends the certificate and refuses to sign without one."},"5196":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/signing-and-encryption-38","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/signing-and-encryption","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/signing-and-encryption#send-the-signature-fields-in-the-build","content":"TLS towards the KMS: in `native` mode the service's KMS client skips certificate verification, and `sign_kms.sh` calls `curl -k`. In `hawkbit` mode the service's own KMS calls verify the certificate, but the SWU signer script still uses `curl -k`. Reach the KMS over an internal address you trust. See Security."},"5197":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/signing-and-encryption-39","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/signing-and-encryption","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/signing-and-encryption#signed-manifests","content":"Each built version also has a **manifest**, an anti-rollback record of what the version contains: name, group, version, packaging, artifacts with their SHA-256, the deliverable and, in `hawkbit` mode, the exact modules and versions that compose the set. A manifest is valid for 5 years (`expires_at`). It is signed with the KMS key when the build carried signing fields, and stored unsigned otherwise (the service logs a warning). If a signing key is configured but the manifest cannot be signed, the build fails."},"5198":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/signing-and-encryption-40","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/signing-and-encryption","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/signing-and-encryption#signed-manifests","content":"Read it with:"},"5199":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/signing-and-encryption-41","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/signing-and-encryption","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/signing-and-encryption#signed-manifests","content":"The response has `manifest` (the exact bytes the signature covers), `signature` (base64 CMS), `algorithm`, `certificate` (PEM), `signed_at` and `expires_at`. In `hawkbit` mode `stale: true` means a signed manifest exists but the set's contents changed since, so the manifest returned describes the set as it is now. The `artifact_signatures` capability reports whether the active backend provides it."},"5200":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/signing-and-encryption-42","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/signing-and-encryption","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/signing-and-encryption#encryption-modes","content":"Mode"},"5201":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/signing-and-encryption-43","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/signing-and-encryption","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/signing-and-encryption#encryption-modes","content":"What you get"},"5202":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/signing-and-encryption-44","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/signing-and-encryption","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/signing-and-encryption#encryption-modes","content":"`native`"},"5203":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/signing-and-encryption-45","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/signing-and-encryption","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/signing-and-encryption#encryption-modes","content":"`hawkbit`"},"5204":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/signing-and-encryption-46","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/signing-and-encryption","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/signing-and-encryption#encryption-modes","content":"None"},"5205":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/signing-and-encryption-47","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/signing-and-encryption","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/signing-and-encryption#encryption-modes","content":"One unencrypted deliverable"},"5206":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/signing-and-encryption-48","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/signing-and-encryption","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/signing-and-encryption#encryption-modes","content":"Yes"},"5207":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/signing-and-encryption-49","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/signing-and-encryption","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/signing-and-encryption#encryption-modes","content":"Yes"},"5208":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/signing-and-encryption-50","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/signing-and-encryption","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/signing-and-encryption#encryption-modes","content":"Shared"},"5209":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/signing-and-encryption-51","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/signing-and-encryption","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/signing-and-encryption#encryption-modes","content":"One deliverable encrypted with one key, served to every device"},"5210":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/signing-and-encryption-52","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/signing-and-encryption","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/signing-and-encryption#encryption-modes","content":"Yes"},"5211":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/signing-and-encryption-53","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/signing-and-encryption","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/signing-and-encryption#encryption-modes","content":"Yes, through the module build endpoints, when the build pipeline is configured"},"5212":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/signing-and-encryption-54","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/signing-and-encryption","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/signing-and-encryption#encryption-modes","content":"Per-device"},"5213":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/signing-and-encryption-55","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/signing-and-encryption","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/signing-and-encryption#encryption-modes","content":"One deliverable per device, each encrypted with that device's own key from SymKMS"},"5214":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/signing-and-encryption-56","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/signing-and-encryption","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/signing-and-encryption#encryption-modes","content":"Yes"},"5215":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/signing-and-encryption-57","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/signing-and-encryption","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/signing-and-encryption#encryption-modes","content":"No"},"5216":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/signing-and-encryption-58","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/signing-and-encryption","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/signing-and-encryption#encryption-modes","content":"The build body decides the mode:"},"5217":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/signing-and-encryption-59","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/signing-and-encryption","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/signing-and-encryption#encryption-modes","content":"**Shared**: send `user`, `encryption_key_name` and `encryption_alg_name`. A `.swu` build is refused without the algorithm. A `.../package` build picks AES-GCM from the key length and only records the name you send."},"5218":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/signing-and-encryption-60","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/signing-and-encryption","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/signing-and-encryption#encryption-modes","content":"**Per-device**: send `encryption_alg_name` **without** `user` or `encryption_key_name`. This holds for `.../package` too: sending the algorithm is what selects per-device mode, and omitting it builds an unencrypted package."},"5219":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/signing-and-encryption-61","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/signing-and-encryption","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/signing-and-encryption#encryption-modes","content":"**None**: send neither."},"5220":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/signing-and-encryption-62","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/signing-and-encryption","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/signing-and-encryption#encryption-modes","content":"Other build fields: `sw_desc_encrypted` also encrypts the sw-description itself, and `selected_artifact_ids` lists the artifacts the build includes. In `native` mode a `.swu` build with no selected artifacts fails."},"5221":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/signing-and-encryption-63","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/signing-and-encryption","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/signing-and-encryption#encryption-modes","content":"In `hawkbit` mode `POST .../swu` returns `501`. Send the same signing and encryption fields to the module build instead: `POST /updates/v1/softwaremodules/by-id/:moduleID/build` (for `swu-build` and `raw` modules). See hawkBit mode."},"5222":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/signing-and-encryption-64","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/signing-and-encryption","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/signing-and-encryption#encryption-modes","content":"The sw-description must mark the artifacts to encrypt with `encrypted = true;`. A per-device build is refused when no artifact is marked, because the key alone does nothing."},"5223":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/signing-and-encryption-65","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/signing-and-encryption","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/signing-and-encryption#algorithms","content":"The `algorithm` of a SymKMS key and the `encryption_alg_name` of a build use these names."},"5224":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/signing-and-encryption-66","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/signing-and-encryption","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/signing-and-encryption#algorithms","content":"Algorithm"},"5225":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/signing-and-encryption-67","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/signing-and-encryption","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/signing-and-encryption#algorithms","content":"Key length"},"5226":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/signing-and-encryption-68","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/signing-and-encryption","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/signing-and-encryption#algorithms","content":"`AES-128-CBC`, `AES-128-CTR`, `AES-128-GCM`"},"5227":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/signing-and-encryption-69","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/signing-and-encryption","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/signing-and-encryption#algorithms","content":"16 bytes"},"5228":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/signing-and-encryption-70","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/signing-and-encryption","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/signing-and-encryption#algorithms","content":"`AES-192-CBC`, `AES-192-CTR`, `AES-192-GCM`"},"5229":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/signing-and-encryption-71","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/signing-and-encryption","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/signing-and-encryption#algorithms","content":"24 bytes"},"5230":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/signing-and-encryption-72","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/signing-and-encryption","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/signing-and-encryption#algorithms","content":"`AES-256-CBC`, `AES-256-CTR`, `AES-256-GCM`"},"5231":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/signing-and-encryption-73","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/signing-and-encryption","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/signing-and-encryption#algorithms","content":"32 bytes"},"5232":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/signing-and-encryption-74","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/signing-and-encryption","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/signing-and-encryption#algorithms","content":"`ASCON-128`, `ASCON-128A`"},"5233":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/signing-and-encryption-75","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/signing-and-encryption","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/signing-and-encryption#algorithms","content":"16 bytes"},"5234":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/signing-and-encryption-76","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/signing-and-encryption","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/signing-and-encryption#algorithms","content":"`ASCON-80PQ`"},"5235":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/signing-and-encryption-77","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/signing-and-encryption","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/signing-and-encryption#algorithms","content":"20 bytes"},"5236":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/signing-and-encryption-78","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/signing-and-encryption","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/signing-and-encryption#algorithms","content":"**SymKMS key names**: matching ignores case, and `_` and `-` are interchangeable (`aes_256_gcm` is stored as `AES-256-GCM`). The separators of the name must still be there: `ascon128a` is not `ASCON-128A`. A key whose length does not match its algorithm is rejected when it is created."},"5237":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/signing-and-encryption-79","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/signing-and-encryption","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/signing-and-encryption#algorithms","content":"**Build names**: `encryption_alg_name` is passed to `swugenerator` as it is. Case is ignored, but the hyphens are required: `aes-256-gcm` works, `AES_256_GCM` is rejected. If the name differs from the algorithm stored with the key, the service logs a warning and uses the name from the request."},"5238":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/signing-and-encryption-80","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/signing-and-encryption","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/signing-and-encryption#algorithms","content":"**`non-swu` packages** (`.../package`, and `hawkbit` `raw` modules) are always encrypted with **AES-GCM**, chosen by key length (16, 24 or 32 bytes). The requested name is only recorded, and a 20-byte Ascon-80pq key is refused. The result is `nonce || ciphertext`."},"5239":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/signing-and-encryption-81","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/signing-and-encryption","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/signing-and-encryption#algorithms","content":"The service generates the IV or nonce. In `native` mode the algorithm and, for shared-key packs, the IV are passed to the device in the WFX job. A per-device build draws a fresh IV for each device and does not record it in the job, so the job carries the algorithm only. The job fields are listed in Connect a device."},"5240":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/signing-and-encryption-82","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/signing-and-encryption","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/signing-and-encryption#create-a-key-per-device","content":"In SymKMS, `POST /symkms/v1/` with `user_id`, an `algorithm` from the table and a `key` (hex or base64) of the right length."},"5241":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/signing-and-encryption-83","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/signing-and-encryption","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/signing-and-encryption#assign-it-to-the-device","content":"`POST /symkms/v1/inventory/:deviceID/keys/:keyID` with a body `{\"purpose\":\"firmware-encryption\"}` and an optional `expires_at` (RFC 3339). A per-device build asks for each device's `firmware-encryption` key."},"5242":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/signing-and-encryption-84","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/signing-and-encryption","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/signing-and-encryption#put-the-same-key-on-the-device","content":"In the form SWUpdate expects (its `-K` key file, with the key, IV and algorithm)."},"5243":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/signing-and-encryption-85","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/signing-and-encryption","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/signing-and-encryption#build","content":"Send `encryption_alg_name` and no `user` or `encryption_key_name`. The sw-description must mark an artifact `encrypted = true;`."},"5244":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/signing-and-encryption-86","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/signing-and-encryption","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/signing-and-encryption#build","content":"**Key purposes.** The conventional purposes are `firmware-encryption`, `config-encryption` and `mac-verification`. The purpose is a placeholder: any value is accepted, and a binding with an empty purpose acts as a wildcard that matches any lookup. This is intentional while per-purpose keys are rolled out. An exact (case-insensitive) match wins over a wildcard, and among equals the most recent assignment wins. Expired or revoked bindings are skipped."},"5245":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/signing-and-encryption-87","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/signing-and-encryption","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/signing-and-encryption#build","content":"**Coverage.** A device with no `firmware-encryption` key is skipped (the reason reads `no firmware-encryption key assigned` for `.swu` builds). The build still succeeds if at least one device was covered, and the pack records the coverage: read `built_device_count`, `total_device_count` and `uncovered_devices` on it. A launch on a pack with uncovered devices is refused with `400`, and there is no override: assign the missing keys and build again. If no device was covered, the build itself fails."},"5246":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/signing-and-encryption-88","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/signing-and-encryption","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/signing-and-encryption#build","content":"**Cost.** A per-device build runs one `swugenerator` process per device, in parallel up to the CPU available to the container. On a 100 MB artifact, one device costs roughly half a second of encryption, plus about three seconds more if the sw-description asks for gzip compression. Size the container accordingly: see Resource sizing. Builds of the same pack are serialized: a second build or version bump while one runs answers `409`."},"5247":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/signing-and-encryption-89","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/signing-and-encryption","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/signing-and-encryption#symkms","content":"SymKMS is the embedded symmetric key service, served by the same process under `/symkms/v1`. It stores keys, assigns them to devices, and can also encrypt, decrypt and compute MACs. Keys are stored in the `symkms` blob store, optionally with at-rest encryption. Create keys with the correct length for their algorithm: random bytes, never a passphrase."},"5248":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/signing-and-encryption-90","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/signing-and-encryption","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/signing-and-encryption#symkms","content":"Task"},"5249":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/signing-and-encryption-91","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/signing-and-encryption","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/signing-and-encryption#symkms","content":"Route"},"5250":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/signing-and-encryption-92","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/signing-and-encryption","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/signing-and-encryption#symkms","content":"Store a key"},"5251":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/signing-and-encryption-93","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/signing-and-encryption","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/signing-and-encryption#symkms","content":"`POST /symkms/v1/`"},"5252":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/signing-and-encryption-94","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/signing-and-encryption","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/signing-and-encryption#symkms","content":"List keys of a user"},"5253":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/signing-and-encryption-95","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/signing-and-encryption","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/signing-and-encryption#symkms","content":"`GET /symkms/v1/?user_id=...`"},"5254":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/signing-and-encryption-96","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/signing-and-encryption","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/signing-and-encryption#symkms","content":"Delete a key"},"5255":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/signing-and-encryption-97","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/signing-and-encryption","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/signing-and-encryption#symkms","content":"`DELETE /symkms/v1/:keyID?user_id=...`"},"5256":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/signing-and-encryption-98","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/signing-and-encryption","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/signing-and-encryption#symkms","content":"Assign or revoke a key for a device"},"5257":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/signing-and-encryption-99","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/signing-and-encryption","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/signing-and-encryption#symkms","content":"`POST` or `DELETE /symkms/v1/inventory/:deviceID/keys/:keyID`"},"5258":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/signing-and-encryption-100","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/signing-and-encryption","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/signing-and-encryption#symkms","content":"A device's active key (privileged, returns key material)"},"5259":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/signing-and-encryption-101","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/signing-and-encryption","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/signing-and-encryption#symkms","content":"`GET /symkms/v1/inventory/:deviceID/key?purpose=...`"},"5260":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/signing-and-encryption-102","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/signing-and-encryption","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/signing-and-encryption#symkms","content":"Which devices use a key"},"5261":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/signing-and-encryption-103","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/signing-and-encryption","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/signing-and-encryption#symkms","content":"`GET /symkms/v1/inventory/by-key/:keyID`"},"5262":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/signing-and-encryption-104","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/signing-and-encryption","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/signing-and-encryption#symkms","content":"A device's key bindings"},"5263":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/signing-and-encryption-105","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/signing-and-encryption","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/signing-and-encryption#symkms","content":"`GET /symkms/v1/inventory/:deviceID`"},"5264":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/signing-and-encryption-106","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/signing-and-encryption","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/signing-and-encryption#symkms","content":"Encrypt, decrypt"},"5265":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/signing-and-encryption-107","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/signing-and-encryption","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/signing-and-encryption#symkms","content":"`POST /symkms/v1/encrypt`, `POST /symkms/v1/decrypt`"},"5266":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/signing-and-encryption-108","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/signing-and-encryption","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/signing-and-encryption#symkms","content":"MAC and verify"},"5267":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/signing-and-encryption-109","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/signing-and-encryption","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/signing-and-encryption#symkms","content":"`POST /symkms/v1/mac`, `POST /symkms/v1/mac/verify` (and the `/file` variants)"},"5268":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/signing-and-encryption-110","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/signing-and-encryption","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/signing-and-encryption#request-bodies","content":"Route"},"5269":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/signing-and-encryption-111","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/signing-and-encryption","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/signing-and-encryption#request-bodies","content":"Body (JSON)"},"5270":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/signing-and-encryption-112","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/signing-and-encryption","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/signing-and-encryption#request-bodies","content":"`POST /symkms/v1/`"},"5271":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/signing-and-encryption-113","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/signing-and-encryption","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/signing-and-encryption#request-bodies","content":"`user_id`, `algorithm`, `key` (hex or base64; hex is tried first), optional `id`. `user_id`, `algorithm` and `key` are required."},"5272":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/signing-and-encryption-114","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/signing-and-encryption","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/signing-and-encryption#request-bodies","content":"`POST /symkms/v1/encrypt`"},"5273":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/signing-and-encryption-115","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/signing-and-encryption","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/signing-and-encryption#request-bodies","content":"`user_id`, `key_name`, `algorithm`, `plaintext` (base64), optional `iv`, optional `format`."},"5274":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/signing-and-encryption-116","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/signing-and-encryption","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/signing-and-encryption#request-bodies","content":"`POST /symkms/v1/decrypt`"},"5275":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/signing-and-encryption-117","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/signing-and-encryption","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/signing-and-encryption#request-bodies","content":"`user_id`, `key_name`, `algorithm`, `ciphertext`, `iv`, optional `format`."},"5276":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/signing-and-encryption-118","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/signing-and-encryption","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/signing-and-encryption#request-bodies","content":"`POST /symkms/v1/mac`"},"5277":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/signing-and-encryption-119","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/signing-and-encryption","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/signing-and-encryption#request-bodies","content":"`user_id`, `key_name`, `mac_algorithm`, `data` (base64). The MAC is returned as hex."},"5278":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/signing-and-encryption-120","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/signing-and-encryption","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/signing-and-encryption#request-bodies","content":"`POST /symkms/v1/mac/verify`"},"5279":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/signing-and-encryption-121","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/signing-and-encryption","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/signing-and-encryption#request-bodies","content":"The same as `/mac`, plus `mac` (hex)."},"5280":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/signing-and-encryption-122","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/signing-and-encryption","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/signing-and-encryption#request-bodies","content":"`format` is `ciphertext` (hex, the default), `base64`, or `cms` (`pkcs7` is an alias): a PEM-encoded CMS structure that embeds the algorithm and IV. With `cms`, `decrypt` can omit `algorithm` and `iv`."},"5281":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/signing-and-encryption-123","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/signing-and-encryption","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/signing-and-encryption#request-bodies","content":"The server generates the nonce for GCM, CTR and Ascon: **a caller-supplied `iv` is refused** for those algorithms. Only CBC accepts one (16 bytes). The response carries the `iv` used (hex)."},"5282":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/signing-and-encryption-124","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/signing-and-encryption","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/signing-and-encryption#request-bodies","content":"`mac_algorithm` is `HMAC-SHA3-256`, `AES-CMAC` or `ASCON-MAC`. The `/file` variants take the data as `multipart/form-data`."},"5283":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/signing-and-encryption-125","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/signing-and-encryption","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/signing-and-encryption#request-bodies","content":"`GET /symkms/v1/:keyID/raw?user_id=...` and `GET /symkms/v1/inventory/:deviceID/key` return raw key material and are privileged: the Updates service itself calls them during a build. The service has no authentication of its own, so restrict these routes at a gateway. See Security."},"5284":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/signing-and-encryption-126","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/signing-and-encryption","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/signing-and-encryption#request-bodies","content":"The same SymKMS routes can run as their own process (`cmd/symkms`) instead of inside the monolith. See Configuration."},"5285":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/troubleshooting","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/troubleshooting","type":"page","content":"Troubleshooting","breadcrumbs":["Docs","Platform","[Enterprise] Updates","Operate"],"tags":[],"url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/troubleshooting"},"5286":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/troubleshooting-0","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/troubleshooting","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/troubleshooting","content":"Symptoms, likely causes and fixes for start-up errors, API calls, builds, downloads and updates that do not reach devices."},"5287":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/troubleshooting-1","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/troubleshooting","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/troubleshooting#http-status-codes","content":"HTTP status codes"},"5288":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/troubleshooting-2","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/troubleshooting","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/troubleshooting#starting-the-service","content":"Starting the service"},"5289":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/troubleshooting-3","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/troubleshooting","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/troubleshooting#api-calls","content":"API calls"},"5290":{"id":"/docs/p