t action steps"],[3309,"hawkBit action, read over DDI"],[2658,"hawkBit actions"],[3718,"hawkBit decides how devices authenticate, not this service. hawkBit 1.1.0 has no anonymous mode: a deployment must enable at least one of the target security token, the gateway security token, or the reverse-proxy header authenticator (`X-Controller-Id` plus `X-Authority`). Pick one and enable it as a hawkBit tenant setting; an installation where all of them are off answers `401` to every device. Recommended for production:"],[3345,"hawkBit decides when a batch is finished. After the last device of a batch reports, hawkBit pauses the rollout, and for a moment its group still reads `running`. The service cannot tell that pause from one an operator made, so a `rollout` call in that window answers `400` with `rollout 1 is paused; resume it first`. Call `resume` and hawkBit releases the next batch itself:"],[5155,"hawkBit does not encrypt artifacts at rest. Enable default encryption in the bucket, or use encrypted (shared-key) packages."],[3724,"hawkBit has its own artifact limits. The image of this repository raises them to 11 GiB per file and 1 TiB in total, to match the default `max_artifact_size_mb` of 10 GiB (`SPRING_SERVLET_MULTIPART_MAXFILESIZE`, `SPRING_SERVLET_MULTIPART_MAXREQUESTSIZE`, `HAWKBIT_SERVER_SECURITY_DOS_MAXARTIFACTSIZE` and `HAWKBIT_SERVER_SECURITY_DOS_MAXARTIFACTSTORAGE`). With stock hawkBit the limit is 1 GiB per file and 20 GiB in total. hawkBit writes an upload to a temporary file first, so give it that much free disk."],[3984,"hawkBit is already your fleet's update backend"],[3743,"hawkBit is its own service with its own database. The Helm chart of this repository does not deploy or manage it."],[2922,"hawkBit itself has no notion of a built module, and this service links only built modules into a hawkBit distribution set. A set is never built directly: `POST .../swu` and `.../package` answer `501` in this mode. The module is built first, in the catalog, and