ing each part separately. See the EST reference."],[1040,"The default response uses the PKCS#7/Base64 format described for cacerts, but contains the issued certificate; do not assume it includes its entire chain. `Accept: application/x-pem-file` returns that certificate in PEM. The client retains the key that signed the CSR."],[325,"The default transport of these clients bounds the dial timeout (30 seconds), the TLS handshake (10 seconds) and idle connection reuse (90 seconds) so an unreachable dependency fails fast instead of hanging; these values are Go transport defaults, not Lamassu settings. HTTP/2 is negotiated when the peer supports it. The authorization-engine connector keeps its own transport without these dial and handshake timeouts; only its overall 30-second request timeout bounds each call."],[2711,"The deliverable exists. The version is immutable. Create a new version to change it."],[1739,"The device client requests a certificate and installs it with the matching key."],[3421,"The device downloads the `uri`, installs it, and reports each step:"],[5516,"The device fails to decrypt"],[780,"The device generates a key and requests a certificate through EST, or an operator assigns it an identity."],[5477,"The device gets `403` from the store after the `302`"],[2070,"The device history relates its previous and current identities. For administrative changes and mutation errors, see Audit logs."],[5510,"The device ignores new deployments"],[5507,"The device installs and shows the old version"],[2091,"The device installs the certificate and the chain it needs."],[3082,"The device is not polling this hawkBit, is not tagged into the group, or cannot authenticate"],[3042,"The device moves its job through the workflow's states, and the workflow decides who may make each move. For the `direct` workflow:"],[3025,"The device must be a member of a Lamassu IoT device group, because a pack belongs to a group and a launch targets the group's devices. In hawkBit mode grou