d VA, and verifies that the UI returns HTML. A passing test confirms basic connectivity, not a full issuance flow."],[2163,"The test should accept an allowed certificate absent from the list and reject it with `certificate revoked` after publishing and using the list containing its serial."],[1437,"The Thing name in the JITP template is derived from `AWS::IoT::Certificate::CommonName`, which corresponds to the device certificate's CN — the same convention as `auto` mode."],[465,"the time scope and affected resources;"],[5727,"The tool is idempotent: keys already in the KMS are skipped, so it can be run several times."],[5418,"The tool rejected its input. Its own message is in the service log"],[5126,"The TTL is short (default 60 s). It bounds when a GET can **start**: a transfer in progress finishes after expiry, and a device that retries or resumes goes back to the static endpoint for a fresh URL. A URL already signed for the same object is reused while it has `min_remaining` validity left (default `min(25s, ttl/2)`); it grants no more than a fresh one."],[3760,"The two backends differ in features. See Capabilities. Notably, `hawkbit` mode has no per-device encryption, no custom workflows, no editing of a launch strategy after creation, no early completion of a campaign, no adding devices to a running campaign, no push events and no set-level prebuilt upload. A `swu-prebuilt` catalog module does accept a finished `.swu`. `native` mode builds one deliverable per pack and has no per-module deliverables."],[3128,"The update packs of every group"],[2633,"The update server"],[4049,"The Updates API is served under `/updates/v1`, and SymKMS under `/symkms/v1`. Paths in this page are relative to `/updates/v1` unless they begin with `/health` or `/symkms`. Behind the Lamassu gateway the prefix is typically `/api/updates/v1`, which is what the dashboard calls."],[2964,"The Updates API, with SymKMS embedded"],[5758,"The upgrade runs in a fixed order: prepare the data and values, run `helm upgrade`, then copy the KMS and VA data into the new volumes. The copy must run after the upgrade, because the destination StatefulSets and PVCs do not exist before it. If you are not upgrading an existing release, go straight to Install with Helm."],[5478,"The URL expired before the device started the GET, the signed `Host` is not what the device used (`public_endpoint` wrong), the signing key cannot read that prefix, or clocks differ"],[2149,"The VA identifies each CRL by the CA’s SKI, and the SKI is derived from its key. Two CAs with the same key have the same SKI and share a single VA role and a single CRL. This happens when a CA is created on an existing KMS key, or when a CA is imported whose certificate declares an SKI already in use. Lamassu takes the SKI of an imported certificate as-is and does not check that it corresponds to its public key. The first CA creates the role and the others keep it."],[2126,"The VA role stores configuration and metadata for the latest list published for a CA’s SKI. Generation requires a usable issuer key; do not assume an imported CA without a key has an available CRL."],[2153,"The VA scheduled job checks every role on each run and requests another list when the remaining validity of `latest_crl` is less than the interval between runs. The frequency is set in Helm with `services.va.job.crl.frequency` (default `0 * * * *`) and accepts a duration (`1h`) or a cron expression. A cron expression is converted into a constant interval equal to the time left until its next firing when the service starts, so it is not aligned with the clock. `refresh_interval` plays no part. Keep `validity` well above the interval: with a shorter validity, the list is regenerated on every cycle."],[2159,"The VA service exposes `GET /crl/{subject_key_id}` without management authorization. Use the **issuing CA’s** SKI, not the end-entity certificate’s SKI or serial. First inspect the certificate’s CDP:"],[5475,"The value has no scheme, or has a path"],[1187,"The value is neither Base64-encoded PEM nor plain PEM: it is a file path or Base64 of non-PEM data. Enter the certificate and key as Base64-encoded PEM, like certificates elsewhere in the API, or as plain PEM (see the webhook settings in DMS). The same message names `mtls_options.key_content` when the key is the offending value."],[118,"The value must be an address handled on the Kubernetes side of the traffic path. If a public EC2 address forwards through WireGuard to the cluster, pass the reachable cluster/VM address, not the EC2 public address."],[5412,"The version has no sw-description (each version needs its own)"],[3605,"The version is already built (create a new version), or another request is building the same pack"],[3440,"The version must be higher than the current one, and the pack keeps its id. The new version starts as `draft`. The artifact links and the module composition carry over, but the sw-description does not: upload it again. Then build with `selected_artifact_ids` (a build replaces the carried links with the ones you select), after uploading a new artifact version if the file changed."],[3583,"The version must be strictly higher than the current one. The new version starts unbuilt and carries the current artifacts forward."],[258,"the version upgrade guides and migration notes in `charts/lamassu/CHANGELOG/` before every upgrade, including the optional CA-to-KMS migration hook described above"],[3845,"The volume mounted at `/data`: build scratch and, by default, local update files."],[675,"The Webhook and Microsoft Teams channels show this configuration in the subscribe form, at the channel step, and again when editing a subscription; Email does not use it. The fields map to the optional `http_client` block described above:"],[1181,"The webhook answered with a redirect. Configure the final absolute `http` or `https` URL in the webhook config; redirects are never followed."],[924,"The webhook authentication modes read `external