re is for the PKI operator replacing an authority in use. You need access to CAs, keys and profiles, a dependency inventory and coordination with trust-store and device owners. Before switching issuance, prepare a test cohort and decide the criterion for ending overlap."],[279,"This requests `192.168.1.50`; it does not claim the IP on your LAN or make it reachable."],[318,"This requires distinct SNI hostnames and cluster networking outside the Lamassu chart."],[1555,"This section connects PKI rules to the device client. Preparation follows this order:"],[2098,"This separation makes it possible to migrate a fleet: you temporarily accept certificates from the old hierarchy, issue with the new one and distribute both chains during the overlap."],[3971,"This service's Postgres, plus WFX"],[2298,"This tab checks whether a signature corresponds to the associated public key."],[2291,"This tab uses the private key to generate a digital signature over a message or an already computed *digest*."],[3236,"Those tiles, the status filter and column are hidden. A set has no build state of its own: it is ready when all its modules are built, and **Start Campaign** stays disabled until then"],[315,"Three independent `LoadBalancer` Services cannot all reserve the same node ports 80 and 443 through K3s ServiceLB. Use one shared Gateway, allocate distinct VIPs with another load-balancer implementation, or use different ports."],[1223,"Three trust relationships"],[5397,"Thresholds are percentages"],[2131,"Time from `thisUpdate` to `nextUpdate`."],[1210,"Timeout or error after issuance"],[1156,"Timeout, HTTP 500 or installation failure"],[4063,"Timeouts"],[4316,"Timestamps"],[371,"TLS"],[5077,"TLS and mTLS (inbound)"],[87,"TLS behavior"],[5079,"TLS to other systems"],[5196,"TLS towards the KMS: in `native` mode the service's KMS client skips certificate verification, and `sign_kms.sh` calls `curl -k`. In `hawkbit` mode the service's own KMS calls verify the certificate, but the SWU signe