,"url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/es/platform/updates/reference/api#symkms","content":"`/symkms/v1/inventory/:deviceID/key?purpose=`"},"4629":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/es/platform/updates/reference/api-610","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/es/platform/updates/reference/api","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/es/platform/updates/reference/api#symkms","content":"La clave en bruto del dispositivo para un propósito, por defecto `firmware-encryption`. Privilegiada. `404` si no hay asociación"},"4630":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/es/platform/updates/reference/api-611","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/es/platform/updates/reference/api","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/es/platform/updates/reference/api#symkms","content":"Un `purpose` vacío es un comodín que coincide con cualquier consulta, y un propósito concreto se compara de forma exacta. Las rutas que devuelven material de clave en bruto confían en que el gateway autentique a quien llama: no las expongas sin mTLS o tokens con ámbito. Consulta Seguridad."},"4631":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/es/platform/updates/reference/api-612","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/es/platform/updates/reference/api","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/es/platform/updates/reference/api#siguientes-pasos","content":"Capabilities para saber qué admite cada backend"},"4632":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/es/platform/updates/reference/api-613","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/es/platform/updates/reference/api","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/es/platform/updates/reference/api#siguientes-pasos","content":"Flujo de actualización con curl, backend native"},"4633":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/es/platform/updates/reference/api-614","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/es/platform/updates/reference/api","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/es/platform/updates/reference/api#siguientes-pasos","content":"Flujo de actualización con curl, backend hawkBit"},"4634":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/es/platform/updates/reference/capabilities","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/es/platform/updates/reference/capabilities","type":"page","content":"Capabilities","breadcrumbs":["Docs","Plataforma","[Enterprise] Actualizaciones","Referencia"],"tags":[],"url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/es/platform/updates/reference/capabilities"},"4635":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/es/platform/updates/reference/capabilities-0","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/es/platform/updates/reference/capabilities","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/es/platform/updates/reference/capabilities","content":"Las 22 capacidades de Lamassu Updates, qué admite cada backend y cómo las lee un cliente."},"4636":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/es/platform/updates/reference/capabilities-1","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/es/platform/updates/reference/capabilities","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/es/platform/updates/reference/capabilities#lee-las-capacidades","content":"Lee las capacidades"},"4637":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/es/platform/updates/reference/capabilities-2","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/es/platform/updates/reference/capabilities","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/es/platform/updates/reference/capabilities#soporte-por-backend","content":"Soporte por backend"},"4638":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/es/platform/updates/reference/capabilities-3","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/es/platform/updates/reference/capabilities","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/es/platform/updates/reference/capabilities#capacidades-condicionales-en-modo-hawkbit","content":"Capacidades condicionales en modo hawkBit"},"4639":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/es/platform/updates/reference/capabilities-4","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/es/platform/updates/reference/capabilities","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/es/platform/updates/reference/capabilities#capacidades-cuyo-significado-cambia","content":"Capacidades cuyo significado cambia"},"4640":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/es/platform/updates/reference/capabilities-5","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/es/platform/updates/reference/capabilities","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/es/platform/updates/reference/capabilities#qué-debe-hacer-un-cliente","content":"Qué debe hacer un cliente"},"4641":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/es/platform/updates/reference/capabilities-6","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/es/platform/updates/reference/capabilities","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/es/platform/updates/reference/capabilities#siguientes-pasos","content":"Siguientes pasos"},"4642":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/es/platform/updates/reference/capabilities-7","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/es/platform/updates/reference/capabilities","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/es/platform/updates/reference/capabilities","content":"`GET /updates/v1/capabilities` indica a un cliente qué backend está activo (`native` o `hawkbit&#x60;) y cuáles de las 22 funciones admite. Léela una vez y oculta lo que no aplique. Una operación que el backend no implementa responde &#x2A;*`501 Not Implemented`**, nunca `500`; un `501` es una propiedad permanente del despliegue, así que reintentar no sirve de nada. La única excepción es `GET /workflows`, que en modo hawkBit responde una lista vacía."},"4643":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/es/platform/updates/reference/capabilities-8","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/es/platform/updates/reference/capabilities","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/es/platform/updates/reference/capabilities#lee-las-capacidades","content":"La ruta no recibe parámetros y no tiene efectos secundarios. El servicio la sirve sin autenticación, igual que `/health`; un gateway delante de él puede seguir exigiendo un token."},"4644":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/es/platform/updates/reference/capabilities-9","page_id":"/docs/pr-prev